</li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>E</strong>xecute with quality</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />If you are passionate about mobile app development and want to work with a company that’s reshaping the industry, Gismart is the place for you. We offer exciting opportunities for professional growth, a supportive and collaborative environment, and the chance to contribute to products that make a tangible impact.<br />For more information about Gismart, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://gismart.com"><u>gismart.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About project</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">FitMe is a fitness app created for people who want to stay active without long, repetitive workouts. It offers short, easy-to-follow routines that can be done at home with no equipment. FitMe is perfect for busy people who want to maintain their health, boost energy levels, and feel good every day — without going to the gym or spending hours on exercise.<br /><br />This is a hands-on, early-stage role. You'll start solo or with a very small team, with your own test budget, and take every hypothesis all the way through: research → test → numbers → decision → scale or kill.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years in Product Marketing, Growth, Growth Product Management, Product or a similar role, ideally in subscription apps or D2C</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of the full user funnel, from acquisition through onboarding and paywall to retention and LTV, and of what drives each metric</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to build your own LTV and payback assumptions without waiting for an analyst</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on track record: you've launched tests yourself, not only managed people who did</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigorous research and prioritization combined with a bias for action: you research to decide, not to find reasons not to move</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership and discipline: you keep your commitments and treat the budget like your own money</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">English at B2 or higher</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Would be a plus:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience launching a product or vertical from 0 to 1</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with new monetization models or non-app products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort using AI and no-code tools for fast prototyping</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate new use cases inside the core product through marketing first, then turn the winners into content and features in the app</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore monetization models and revenue streams beyond the current ones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find and validate hypotheses that could become standalone products, inside or outside Health &amp; Fitness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Research markets, trends, competitors and user behavior, and turn the findings into a prioritized list of bets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build business cases with LTV and unit-economics assumptions, and define success and stop criteria before spending money</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch tests yourself: run campaigns, vibe-code landing pages and prototypes, run surveys and user interviews</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the budget, timelines and commitments for every experiment, and report results honestly, including the ones that fail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring in design, product, analytics and marketing once a bet has earned more resources</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like in 6 months</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A steady pipeline of tested hypotheses, each with clear numbers and a decision</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one direction validated and moving toward scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test budgets spent with discipline, with every dollar traceable to something we learned</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is not for you if</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer strategy decks to hands-on execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You need a large team and established processes to be effective</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're uncomfortable when most experiments don't work out</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-First Culture:</strong> Work from wherever you're most productive, with an office in Kyiv for those who prefer it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coworking Compensation:</strong> We cover coworking costs: 100% in Ukraine (except Kyiv) and 50% worldwide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Free Office Lunches:</strong> Enjoy free lunches whenever you work from our office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Public Holidays Policy:</strong> 12 public holidays a year, accrued monthly, to use when it suits you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sick Leave Support:</strong> 100% paid sick leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mental and Physical Health:</strong> Medical insurance after the probation period, plus sport and psychologist session compensation from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equipment Support:</strong> We provide the equipment you need to do your best work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning and Development:</strong> We cover 70% of professional development courses and 100% of corporate English courses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off:</strong> 18 paid working days plus 3 personal days a year, plus one extra day for each year with Gismart.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Corporate Events:</strong> Team gatherings and company events to connect beyond work.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/gismart/remote-growth-rd-lead-fitme-137268","tags":["FitMe"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1795696814},{"slug":"analytics-engineer-data-platform-hamburg-or-berlin-437592","company_name":"Statista","title":"Analytics Engineer - Data Platform (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>Statista</strong>, we’re all about facts and data, for we are the world's leading business data platform. By providing reliable and easy-to-use data as well as various data analytics products and services, we empower people worldwide to make fact-based decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Hamburg in 2007, we have quickly grown into a global company with offices in major cities such as London, New York, Berlin and Tokyo. And we still have a lot of plans. Our constant growth does not only prove our success, but also keeps creating new development and career opportunities for our employees.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value and celebrate our diverse culture. You are welcome here for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or whether you prefer bar graphs to pie charts. Your story matters – keep writing it as part of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to join us?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join Statista’s newly formed Data Platform team. We’re building a central platform that brings together data—from market statistics to consumer surveys—under consistent standards for quality, documentation, and access. This gives product teams and AI agents a trusted foundation to build new applications and features without duplicating data or setting up separate pipelines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, implement, and maintain backend services in Python that power our data access and distribution layer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and operate automated build, test, and deployment pipelines following CI/CD and GitOps practices, running on AWS and Kubernetes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and maintain data models and schemas (Avro, SQL) for our data pipelines and services, and publish them to downstream consumers via our Kafka-based distribution platform and schema registry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build access-layer data models in our analytics environment (e.g., Snowflake) so applications can work with the data directly, including via API</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the coordination interface between the Data and Tech divisions, aligning priorities, schemas, and timelines across upstream and downstream teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4+ years of experience in analytics engineering, data engineering, or a related role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong SQL skills and solid experience in data modeling (e.g., dimensional modeling, star schemas).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with event streaming and message distribution, ideally Kafka, including schema management with the Kafka schema registry (Avro, Protobuf, or JSON Schema).</p></li><l