en't looking, and your current role has started to feel a little too comfortable.</span></p><h3></h3><p><span style="color: #121317">At eleQtron, you can still help write our next chapter and decide how we get there. We build quantum computers, with about 130 people across Hamburg and Siegen. Most of the people we need are physicists, engineers and software specialists who are sought-after talent. We’re still shaping how eleQtron finds them, how it tells them why they should join, and how we evolve our approach to hiring. That's the job you can define.</span></p><br /><br /><h4>What you'll do</h4><ul><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You'll sit inside our technical teams as their talent partner. You'll learn how each team works, where it’s strong and where the gaps are. You'll shape the brief and the bar with the hiring manager, pushing back where you have to.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You'll run our hardest searches yourself, from mapping the market to closing the offer and helping people relocate. Most of those hires will be people you found rather than people who applied.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">With the team, you'll work out why a strong scientist or engineer should join eleQtron, and you'll make sure the people we want to hire hear it, through universities, conferences and research networks as well as the usual (and unusual) channels.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You'll build the way we hire: structured interviews, scorecards and debriefs that every technical team uses, with the data to show whether they work. You'll coach our hiring managers and interviewers to that standard.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You'll have the freedom  to be creative in how you source, and to use AI for the research and admin, so your time goes on judgement and on conversations with people.</span></p></li></ul><p style=";"></p><h4>This is for you if</h4><ul><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You've outgrown your current role and want to build something.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You start things without waiting to be asked, and you finish them.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You move with urgency when the picture is still unclear.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You'd rather shape an employer brand than inherit one.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">Hard technical searches interest you more than easy ones.</span></p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><p><span style="color: #121317">You don't need to have built a recruiting function before. If you have, that helps, but what matters more is your appetite to continually improve and push us forward. If you haven't, we care more that take initiative without being asked and you to and seen it through, taking the time to learn what worked, or not.</span></p><p style=";"></p><p style=";"></p><h4>What’s worth knowing</h4><p><span style="color: #121317">Our People team has a lot to deliver. You'll build while you hire, and the hiring won't wait for the building to finish. Some searches will take months, and the people you talk to will be comparing us with big tech and research labs. You'll also spend regular time at both our Hamburg and Siegen sites.</span></p><p style=";"></p><p><span style="color: #121317">So this probably isn't for you if:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You want a settled process to run.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You're happy with the way things are and want to keep them that way.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You'd rather someone else decided how hiring should work.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You need a clear path with little ambiguity.</span></p></li></ul><p style=";"></p><h3><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color: #121317">You've recruited scarce technical specialists from start to finish: findin