as a leading force transforming the market.</p><p>Our SAP-certified platform provides the full digital infrastructure for forming and operating Vicos: marketing, finance, legal, organization – increasingly enhanced by AI agents as productive Vico members.</p><p>We are scaling our go-to-market and need a leader who shapes how enterprises source professional services in the agentic era.</p><p><strong>Our offer to you</strong></p><p>As Business Development Director you combine three capabilities:</p><ul><li><p>strategic consulting which helps clients buy the right professional services product in the right way – that is how selling works for our product</p></li><li><p>understanding AI’s role in service delivery</p></li><li><p>entrepreneurial drive in building a hyper-scaling business: this is about continuously driving the perfection of our product, go-to-market, processes and tools</p></li></ul><p>You challenge how your clients source, deliver and scale professional services – and you show to them why the Vico model is structurally superior (when this is the case, which it most often is). You operate as a trusted advisor at C-level, translating Vicoland’s platform and AI capabilities into client-specific value scenarios.</p><p>You join our leadership team with end-to-end accountability: from market shaping and first pitch to delivery oversight and long-term account growth. You supervise the Vicos serving your clients – acting as an entrepreneur leading entrepreneurs.</p><h2>Tasks</h2><p><strong>Shape the market</strong></p><ul><li><p>Position Vicoland with enterprise clients as the strategic alternative to traditional professional services models.</p></li><li><p>Question established sourcing models and demonstrate why Vicos deliver better outcomes.</p></li><li><p>Plan and implement mixed human / AI offers by Vicos.</p></li><li><p>Develop go-to-market strategies tailored to specific client contexts.</p></li><li><p>Build thought leadership through events and LinkedIn presence.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Win and grow clients</strong></p><ul><li><p>Develop and own a portfolio of enterprise clients and partners – from strategic outreach through close to long-term expansion.</p></li><li><p>Conduct consultative, insight-driven conversations at C-level. Translate the Vico model into concrete ROI scenarios for each client.</p></li><li><p>Identify cross- and upsell opportunities with a founder’s mindset. Build pipeline strategically, not only transactionally.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Lead Vicos in delivery</strong></p><ul><li><p>Supervise and coach Vico Leads in your client group – hold them accountable for delivery quality and commercial performance.</p></li><li><p>Activate new Vico Leads and set them up for success. Step in when needed to protect client relationships.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Drive AI into Business Development</strong></p><ul><li><p>Integrate Vicoland’s AI and agentic capabilities into client conversations – position the Vicoland platform and Vicos as AI-first.</p></li><li><p>Use AI tools actively in your own work and contribute to the evolution of AI-powered Vico members.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Shape the company</strong></p><ul><li><p>Contribute to Vicoland’s strategy as a member of the leadership team.</p></li><li><p>Bring market intelligence, client feedback, and competitive insight into the organization.</p></li><li><p>Help define how we scale – processes, tools, talent, culture.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>5+ years in professional services – e. g. in consulting, system integration, or in sales roles for complex products.</p></li><li><p>Consultative selling capacity: you can win complex enterprise deals by advising, not pitching.</p></li><li><p>Challenger mindset: you shape how clients and the market at large think about professional services sourcing and are comfortable challenging senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>AI-affinity: you actively use AI tools and understand the strategic implications of agentic AI for professional services.</p></li><li><p>Entrepreneurial energy – you are drawn to building markets, not administering existing ones. Own entrepreneurial experience is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p>Experience leading teams or practices – you have managed people, not just projects.</p></li><li><p>Strong academic background, fast career progression, proven commercial impact.</p></li><li><p>Fluent in German and English (DACH is our home market, while we expand internationally).</p></li><li><p>Network power: you have and build valuable relationships easily.</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Attractive compensation with fixed salary, variable component tied to the commercial success of your Vicos, and company shares (ESOP in place).</p></li><li><p>Entrepreneurial key position in an industry-transforming company with direct impact on company results, the market, and your personal growth.</p></li><li><p>High degree of autonomy in how you develop your client portfolio and lead your Vico group.</p></li><li><p>Fast-paced environment with a highly talented team of diverse backgrounds and top-notch qualifications.</p></li><li><p>Flexibility in how and where you work – remote and/or from one of our offices (Frankfurt, Barcelona, Berlin, Seville).</p></li></ul><p><strong>Ready to shape a market? Then let’s talk about your journey as Business Development Director.</strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/vicoland/business-development-director-excel-as-entrepreneur-through-strategy-sales-and-ai-berlin-61211","tags":["Business Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","executive"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795689054},{"slug":"mid-senior-full-stack-ai-product-engineer-berlin-352833","company_name":"Spatial Commerce Ltd","title":"Mid-Senior Full-Stack AI Product Engineer","description":"<h2>Mid-Senior Full-Stack AI Product Engineer</h2><h2>About Oda</h2><p>Spatial Commerce builds Oda AI, a platform that turns real spaces into ground-truthed world models. Creating the spatial layer that AI and software plug into to understand and act on the built environment.The AI behind it runs in production: a conversational space planner that proposes layouts and waits for approval before applying them, vision pipelines that locate objects in 3D captures, GPU rendering services, and retrieval over scene knowledge.</p><p>We recently raised €1.5M from AI & PropTech investors and have licensed technology from a well known German research institute. We’re looking for a full-stack engineer who can multiply what a small team ships. You’ll work with a team of five engineers, the CEO and the CPO on product decisions, and customers.</p><h2>What you’ll own</h2><ul><li><p>Planner and assistant. Improve how the in-viewer planner interprets requests, proposes options and checks collisions before a change is approved. Decide which requests need a model and which need a deterministic query.</p></li><li><p>Vision and GPU pipelines. Run and improve the services that render captures, segment objects and match catalogue items to scanned spaces. These run on Cloud and making them scale is an open problem.</p></li><li><p>Evaluation. Build and maintain the evals that decide whether a model or prompt change is safe to ship, and extend CI coverage beyond today’s agent tool-call checks.</p></li><li><p>Scaling and cost. Keep latency and per-document cost under control as usage grows, across LLM calls, GPU jobs, and the graph and vector stores behind them.</p></li><li><p>Architecture calls. Choose tools, frameworks and code structure, and own the reasoning. Some of the open questions are model routing per scene and where the Graph DB read model should stop being rebuildable.</p></li><li><p>Product sense. Turn a vague customer need into a shipped feature, and say when the answer is not an AI feature at all.</p></li><li><p>AI-Assisted Operations: Use AI tools to help build, automate, and maintain our infrastructure, and help shape how the team uses them.</p></li></ul><h2>Our stack</h2><p>Cloud: Google Cloud Platform. Production and staging are separate GCP projects, with services in a European region.</p><p>Frontend: Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Turborepo monorepo, PlayCanvas and three.js for 3D, next-intl across 15 locales.</p><p>AI: Genkit with Gemini and OpenAI-compatible providers, routing across model providers, embedding-based retrieval, VLM and Foundation Models.</p><p>Backend: Firebase on GCP (Firestore, Storage, Auth, App Hosting, App Check), Firebase Functions, Neo4j as a rebuildable graph and vector read Docker.</p><p>Compute: Python services on Cloud Run, Cloud Run Jobs triggered per document, gsplat and PyTorch/CUDA, Blender scripting for room authoring.</p><p>Delivery: GitHub Actions, Cloud Build, Secret Manager, Playwright and Jest, load tests against staging and production, PostHog for product analytics.</p><h2>What you bring</h2><h2>Required</h2><ul><li><p>Years of Experience: Six or more years building production software, including at least two years in infrastructure, SRE, DevOps, or platform engineering.</p></li><li><p>Education: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p>Core Technical Skills: Strong TypeScript and React, and comfort in Python for model-serving or data work.</p></li><li><p>Infrastructure as Code: Experience managing infrastructure as code with tools such as Terraform, Pulumi, or similar.</p></li><li><p>CI/CD: Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines in Github, GitHub Actions, or similar.</p></li><li><p>Cloud: Hands on experience with Google Cloud, Firebase or a similar managed stack.</p></li><li><p>Experience running GPU or other compute-heavy workloads in production, including queueing, retries, timeouts and cost control.</p></li><li><p>You have architected or helped build out an early-stage product until hundreds of thousands of people used it daily. You can name the decisions that got it there and the ones you’d make differently.</p></li><li><p>A habit of writing evals or measurable acceptance checks before trusting a model change.</p></li><li><p>You have made hard calls on tools and code and can defend them: what to keep, what to delete, and when a simpler approach beats a clever one.</p></li></ul><h2>Strongly preferred</h2><ul><li><p>Experience with LLM agents that use tools, structured outputs or retrieval over domain data.</p></li><li><p>Graph databases (Neo4j or similar) and vector indexes at scale.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Firestore security rules and server-side authorization, where admin credentials bypass client rules.</p></li><li><p>Real product ownership: you have talked to users, made tradeoffs in a spec, and shipped something you then had to maintain.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul><li><p>Experience with 3D data: sfM, Pointcloud, 3D Gaussian Splatting.</p></li><li><p>Blender Python, PlayCanvas or three.js in a production app.</p></li></ul><h2>How you’ll work</h2><ul><li><p>We ship constantly and keep a short constitution that every change must respect. You’ll read it on day one and help improve it. It favours simple code, surgical changes and verifiable success criteria.</p></li><li><p>You write the spec, the test and the rollout plan, not only the code.</p></li><li><p>You own the on-call for your features and the metrics that show they work.</p></li><li><p>You decide when a problem needs a model and when it needs a database query, and you can explain that decision to a customer.</p></li></ul><h2>Location & Work Model</h2><p>This role is based in our Berlin - Alexanderplatz or Berlin - Charlottenburg office. We work in a high-collaboration environment and ask team members to be on-site a minimum of 3 days per week.</p><h2>Compensation & Benefits</h2