&lt;p&gt;If you want to know more about how Fever processes your personal data, click here&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cIzPP7QJGht5LAGKkRGQP8fxh-Z4Mfph2JhGSvhd8zM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.y7rpsj7nzave&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Fever - Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/feverup/event-coordinator-osnabruck-working-student-freelancer-part-time-osnabruck-lower-saxony-55629","tags":["FOs (DACH)"],"job_types":[],"location":"Osnabrück, Lower Saxony","created_at":1795686916},{"slug":"partner-marketing-manager-dach-deutsche-telekom-germany-185718","company_name":"Horizon3Ai","title":"Partner Marketing Manager, DACH – Deutsche Telekom","description":"<h1>Partner Marketing Manager, DACH – Deutsche Telekom</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Germany (remote)<br /><strong>Languages:</strong> German and English (fluent)<br /><strong>Travel:</strong> Regional travel as required across CEE/EMEA</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a> is seeking a results-driven Demand Generation Marketing Manager to build and execute joint marketing with Deutsche Telekom (DT), supporting growth across its B2B business in CEE. This role turns shared commercial priorities into practical, measurable marketing programs that help DT and Horizon3 create demand, engage customers, equip partner teams, and grow pipeline for cybersecurity services built around the NodeZero™ platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with the Deutsche Telekom business unit director, channel sales, regional sales, and EMEA marketing, you will connect partner strategy to execution. You will shape joint plans, coordinate stakeholders across both organisations, and measure what marketing contributes—from partner engagement and qualified leads through to pipeline and revenue influence. This is a hands-on role for someone who can navigate a complex partner environment and make progress through influence rather than direct authority.</p><h2>About Horizon3</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Horizon3 is a fast-growing cybersecurity company on a mission to help organisations find, fix, and verify exploitable attack paths before attackers exploit them. Its flagship NodeZero™ platform delivers production-safe autonomous penetration testing and other security assessment capabilities across internal, external, cloud, and hybrid environments. NodeZero is used by organisations ranging from small institutions to Global 100 enterprises, as well as by security teams, consultants, and managed service providers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and own a joint marketing plan with Deutsche Telekom that translates its B2B priorities, target segments, sales campaigns, and managed security service goals into an actionable campaign calendar, audience strategy, and investment plan aligned with Horizon3 DACH and EMEA growth objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align campaign outcomes, ownership, timelines, success measures, and follow-up with the business unit director and DT stakeholders; build effective relationships across DT marketing, sales, channel, and service teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop trusted working relationships across DT marketing, sales, channel, and relevant service teams, coordinating decisions and execution across a large, matrixed organisation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver integrated, German-language campaigns for DT’s B2B audiences across events, roundtables, webinars, digital, account-based marketing, partner communications, and sales plays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Localise Horizon3 messaging for the German market and coordinate end-to-end execution across both organisations, including briefs, content, approvals, vendors, schedules, and event logistics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support joint customer engagement and co-selling with account-specific programs and coordinated sales follow-up.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop demand-generation programs that support DT’s reseller, service-provider, and managed security service motions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and manage market development funds (MDF) and other co-marketing investment in line with agreed priorities, budgets, governance, and campaign objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run enablement programmes, alongside the Horizon3 Channel Team to equip DT sales and partner teams with clear NodeZero positioning, customer value, campaign offers, and calls to action.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate campaign enablement with channel, product marketing, and solutions engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track partner engagement, lead quality, conversion, sourced and influenced pipeline, and campaign return.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share performance insights and recommendations in regular updates and quarterly business reviews, and contribute successful programs to EMEA playbooks.</p></li></ul><h2>What You’ll Bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years of experience in B2B technology marketing, with substantial experience in partner/channel marketing, field marketing, or demand generation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with telco resellers, telecommunications providers, systems integrators, distributors, MSSPs/MSPs, or comparable indirect routes to market—and/or a strong background i