uspr.de">Knuspr.de</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Kifli.hu">Kifli.hu</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Gurkerl.at">Gurkerl.at</a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Sezamo.ro">Sezamo.ro</a>, choosing from over 20,000 items delivered within hours in 15-minute windows. We provide in all our countries a superior customer experience and the freshest food from local farmers and artisans, as well as a broad supermarket selection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re now taking our dedication to quality even further by centralising our approach across all markets, elevating our standards and driving higher expectations in the industry. To spearhead this mission, we’re introducing the role of Director of Quality, who will oversee quality assurance operations across all regions, unify processes, and set new benchmarks for industry excellence.<em><br /></em></p><h2><strong>Why this role is exciting</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br /></strong>The Director of Quality will face the ambitious challenge of upholding and unifying industry-leading quality standards that not only meet but surpass local regulatory requirements across all markets. Meeting these high standards is essential to maintaining customer satisfaction and trust, from supplier assurance to final product delivery.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct customer and business impact:</strong> Your standards decide what lands in more than a million customers’ kitchens, directly driving satisfaction, complaints, refunds, and shrink across all five markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build it from the ground up:</strong> This is a new Group role. You will centralise quality across five countries into one function with one set of standards that go beyond local regulation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True ownership with zero friction:</strong> No long or cumbersome approval processes between a good idea and the warehouse floor; if it works in a pilot, you scale it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tech and AI-first environment:</strong> We build all our technology in-house, so you can embed quality checks directly into our systems, automate manual controls, and use data and AI to catch issues before customers do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct executive exposure:</strong> Reporting directly to the Group COO, you will have the mandate and space to shape how quality works across the whole company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will own and deliver</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business outcomes:</strong> Own the quality results of the Group; customer quality feedback scores, quality-related complaints and refunds, audit outcomes, and quality-driven shrink, setting targets with country leads and tracking impact in operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unified standards:</strong> Establish and enforce one set of quality standards across the Czech Republic, Germany, Austria, Hungary, and Romania that exceed local regulatory requirements and set the benchmark for the industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end quality assurance:</strong> Lead quality from supplier selection and onboarding, through inbound inspection, storage, and handling in our fulfillment centers, all the way to delivery at the customer’s door—including our own-label range and Farm-to-Door products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Risk-based quality management &amp; automation:</strong> Build proactive, risk-based systems that catch issues before they escalate, replace manual checks with automation, and turn data from customers, audits, and operations into actionable improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"