trong></h3><p class="MsoNormal">As a Site Reliability Engineer, you'll work at the intersection of platform engineering, AI-driven tooling and security by design. Together with your team, you'll build the framework to package and deploy software solutions on top of OPCP - turning vague product ideas into repeatable, observable and self-healing services. You'll work on the conception, automation and operation of the platform, drive continuous improvements and help new teams onboard with the framework and OPCP. Working hand in hand with developers, security specialists and AI researchers, you keep an overview in ambiguous situations, analyze systems and make well-founded decisions based on that analysis.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">AI-assisted engineering is part of our daily toolchain because it materially improves how we build and operate the platform – from spec-driven development with LLM assistance and knowledge-base-driven retrieval for incident response and design to agentic coding workflows and faster runbook authoring and review. We are investing in this direction as a structural part of our engineering practice and are looking for teammates who already work this way – not because it is trendy, but because they have seen it compound their own output.<br></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#ffffff">Your Tasks</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Design, build and maintain the <strong>Cloud Store packaging framework</strong> that standardizes how software is delivered on OPCP.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Extend and evolve the <strong>AI substrate</strong> - LLM-driven code assistants, knowledge-base retrieval and agentic coding hooks - that amplifies our engineering output.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Create and curate <strong>agentic coding environments</strong>: custom agents and sub-agents, slash commands, hooks and prompt engineering pipelines that become everyday developer tools.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Own the <strong>knowledge-base layer</strong> that powers AI-driven incident response, design assistance and runbook generation.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Drive our <strong>Kubernetes stack</strong> forward and implement robust <strong>GitOps pipelines</strong> (FluxCD / ArgoCD) for continuous delivery.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Write, publish and continuously improve <strong>OPCP onboarding runbooks and best-practice guides</strong> for internal product teams.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Analyze opaque system behavior, surface <strong>root causes</strong> and deliver concrete, data-backed improvement proposals - even when initial requirements are unclear.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Develop, version and operate the <strong>Infrastructure as Code</strong> stack (Terraform, Ansible) that underpins the platform, and take part in our <strong>on-call rotation</strong>.<br></p></li></ul><h3><strong>What we offer you💼</strong></h3><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraph"><strong>AI-augmented engineering as a first-class workflow</strong> - including agentic coding tooling, knowledge bases as the backbone of our AI workflows and room to push our engineering practices further</p></li><li><p>Exceptional team spirit across all departments and national borders; we live #OneTeam</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraph">Exciting work in a highly innovative and international environment with cutting-edge technologies</p></li><li><p>32 vacation days, increasing with length of service</p></li><li><p>Flexible working hours, home office options, and a secure permanent position with market- and performance-based compensation</p></li><li><p>Employer-funded pension plan and an attractive insurance package</p></li><li><p>OVHcloud covers 50% of public transportation costs</p></li><li><p>Up to €400 annual financial contribution from OVHcloud towards sports activities (gym membership, sports classes, etc.)</p></li><li><p>Through Corporate Benefits, you receive attractive discounts at numerous shops and companies</p></li><li><p>We contribute to the leasing of your cargo bike</p></li><li><p>Regular company events and free cold and hot beverages</p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>4+ years of experience in infrastructure or platform engineering</strong>, ideally in a security-focused, highly automated environment</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Proven practice of AI-assisted engineering</strong> - you use LLMs for spec-driven development, runbook authoring or agentic coding and have seen it compound your own output</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Deep knowledge of <strong>Linux/Unix internals</strong>, system administration and performance tuning</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Hands-on experience with <strong>OpenStack</strong> (or a comparable cloud platform) for infrastructure provisioning and management</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Strong skills in <strong>Infrastructure as Code</strong> with <strong>Terraform and Ansible</strong> and the ability to model complex environments as code</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">A solid background in <strong>Kubernetes</strong> and <strong>GitOps workflows</strong> (FluxCD / ArgoCD) as well as in designing and maintaining <strong>CI/CD pipelines</strong></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Hands-on experience with modern <strong>observability stacks</strong> - metrics, logs and traces</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Proficiency in <strong>scripting and automation</strong> with <strong>Python, Bash and Go</strong></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">A solid grasp of <strong>security fundamentals</strong> (IAM, secrets management, hardening, compliance) and <strong>distributed systems concepts</strong> (CAP theorem, consensus, fault tolerance)</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">A clear <strong>bias toward automation over manual toil</strong>, a passion for <strong>continuous improvement</strong> and strict <strong>documentation discipline</strong></p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">You thrive in <strong>collaborative product teams</strong>, bring a strong <strong>ownership mentality</strong>, a <strong>blameless culture mindset</strong> and <strong>strong communication skills</strong>, and you adapt easily when things change</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/gridscale-gmbh/site-reliability-engineer-ai-assisted-platform-kubernetes-koln-373595","tags":["Development"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Köln, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Deutschland","created_at":1795685480},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-iam-billing-koln-435518","company_name":"gridscale GmbH","title":"Senior Software Engineer- IAM & Billing (m/f/d)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">At our company, it's all about #OneTeam! Join gridscale and help shape the future of the cloud together with OVH.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">As a leading tech company, we've been working for over two decades to reduce our environmental footprint - with innovative solutions and an open cloud designed to be sustainable from the ground up: #SustainableByDesign.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">Every tenant, every user, every permission on our sovereign cloud runs through the services this squad builds, and so does every euro that gets billed. We are the Business Logic squad in the Cloud Store team at gridscale, part of OVHcloud, and we build the backend layer of OPCP, our On-Prem Cloud Platform: identity and access management, consumption tracking and billing for enterprise customers who run their cloud on their own premises, often fully air-gapped. Our first fully integrated release is out, and the next step is taking it to production grade, while the platform is becoming the foundation on which other OVHcloud products build their sovereign offerings. The design decisions this squad makes over the next year will shape all of that, and we want you in the room when they are made.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">Our Tech Stack&nbsp;🚀</span></strong></h4><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">· AI Coding Agents &amp; Agentic Workflows · Python (async) · REST · PostgreSQL · Redis</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">· Docker · Kubernetes · OAuth2/OIDC · Keycloak · OpenStack<br></span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Your Role💻</span></strong></h3><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">As a senior engineer in the squad, you own backend services end to end, from the first design sketch to running in production on Kubernetes. You make architecture calls in a domain where correctness, security and backward compatibility are not optional: billing can't be "roughly right", and an auth bug is a security incident. You write down the decisions that matter, review your teammates' designs and code, and help the whole squad raise its engineering bar. We write code to be read: clear, maintainable and easy for the next person – human or agent – to change. Our tests exist to catch real bugs, not to turn the coverage badge green. On-call is shared across the squad, and our working language is English – no German required.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#121317">For us, AI is a structural shift in how software is built, not an add-on. Agentic development runs through our entire lifecycle, from specification and design through implementation, testing and code review: AI agents do much of the work, while engineers set the direction, define the guardrails and own every merge. AI-assisted is our default - agents generate, engineers decide, every change is human-reviewed before it merges, and accountability always stays with the engineer. You already work this way every day and operate at the frontier of these tools: you know where agents excel, where they fail, and how to build workflows that deliver production-grade results in a domain where correctness and security are non-negotiable. With us, you'll push this practice further across the squad and beyond.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Your Tasks</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p class="MsoListParagraph"><span style="color:#121317">Design and build </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Python services</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> for </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">IAM</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">consumption tracking</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">billing</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> on OPCP, using AI agents across the full development lifecycle.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraph"><span style="color:#121317">Own your services </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">end to end</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, from the first design sketch to </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">production on Kubernetes</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, and share </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">on-call</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> with the squad.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraph"><span style="color:#121317">Shape the squad's </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">agentic engineering practice</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: agent workflows, context and guardrails, </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">review standards for AI-generated code</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, and how we measure the impact.</span></p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraph"><span style="color:#121317">Design our <