h-419862","company_name":"Wordsmith","title":"Finance Associate","description":"<h2><strong>Finance Associate</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Edinburgh | Full-time </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wordsmith</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legal touches everything that matters in a business: every deal, every hire, every launch, every risk. Sales runs on Salesforce. Engineering runs on GitHub. In-house legal runs on inboxes, chat threads and tools that weren’t built for it.<br />Wordsmith is changing that. We’re building the platform in-house legal runs on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requests from across the business come in through one front door. AI agents handle the routine work. Lawyers stay in control where judgment matters. Legal finally gets to triage by risk, not by whoever shouted loudest.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re built for in-house teams, not law firms. Our customers want to spend less on outside counsel, not more, and we’re on their side of that equation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">More than 500 companies run on Wordsmith, including Financial Times, Canva, Trip.com, Revolut, Adyen, Trustpilot, and Sage. We’ve raised $100M from Index Ventures, General Catalyst, Highland Europe and others, and we’re growing fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our office in Edinburgh.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why this role is different</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You won’t be joining a big, process-heavy finance function. You’ll be one of the founding Finance hires, working on a brand new, AI-native ERP system (Rillet) with the freedom to actually improve how things are done — not just keep the lights on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />If you want real exposure to the business, a seat close to the founders and leadership team, and the chance to shape processes rather than inherit them, this is that seat.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Finance Assistant, you’ll own the day-to-day mechanics that keep Wordsmith’s finances running — cash, invoicing, collections, payables and expenses — and you’ll have the tools and the licence to automate as much of it as possible.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete daily cash reconciliation across our accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up customer contracts in our ERP (Rillet) and issue invoices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chase accounts receivable to keep debtor days down</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own all accounts payable activity, including uploading bills and creating payment runs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help with month end balance sheet reconciliations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help administer our travel and expense system and be the first point of contact for queries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pick up other finance tasks as they come up — in a small team, that’s part of the job</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have access to a wide range of AI tools to optimise and automate tasks and find new ways of doing things</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you might be</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re not looking for someone who wants a narrow, ticket-based role. You might be:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified and looking for a new challenge in an exciting fast moving industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Newly qualified and ready to take real ownership from day one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Looking for broader exposure than a larger finance function gives you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Someone who’s used to (or excited about) using modern tools and automation rather than doing everything by hand</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Someone who understands the importance of getting things right and really being a team player</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">What matters most is being highly motivated and genuinely keen to get stuck in quickly — we’ll help you grow into the rest.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Newly qualified (ACCA preferred but AAT also considered)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable owning process end-to-end — cash, invoicing, AR, AP and expenses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Happy working in-office five days a week in central Edinburgh</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about tech and automation, and keen to use it to improve how finance runs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organised, with the judgement to know when something needs chasing</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is on-site five days a week, from our office in central Edinburgh — a short walk from both Waverley and Haymarket. You’ll sit inside a small finance team, which means direct exposure to the wider business rather than being several layers removed from it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a fast-moving environment with light process and a genuine bias toward using technology to remove manual work, not add to it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you can expect</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real ownership over core finance processes from day one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with a brand new, AI-native ERP system (Rillet)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close exposure to a small finance team and the wider business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The freedom to use an extensive suite of tech tools to improve and automate how things are done</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Wordsmith</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a fast-moving, Edinburgh-based Legal AI company that’s just raised $100M. Joining now means joining early enough to shape how our finance function is built — with modern tools, real ownership, and a team that wants to do things properly rather than just keep pace.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wordsmith/finance-associate-edinburgh-419862","tags":["G&A"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Edinburgh","created_at":1795750985},{"slug":"head-of-product-marketing-london-204404","company_name":"Wordsmith","title":"Head of Product Marketing","description":"<h1><strong>Head of Product Marketing </strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">London | New York </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wordsmith</strong><br />Legal touches everything that matters in a business: every deal, every hire, every launch, every risk. Sales runs on Salesforce. Engineering runs on GitHub. In-house legal runs on inboxes, chat threads and tools that weren't built for it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wordsmith is changing that. We're building the platform in-house legal runs on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requests from across the business come in through one front door. AI agents handle the routine work. Lawyers stay in control where judgment matters. Legal finally gets to triage by risk, not by whoever shouted loudest.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're built for in-house teams, not law firms. Our customers want to spend less on outside counsel, not more, and we're on their side of that equation. More than 500 companies run on Wordsmith, including Financial Times, Canva, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Trip.com">Trip.com</a>, Starling, Safelite and Sage. We've raised $100M from Index Ventures, General Catalyst, Highland Europe and others, and we're growing fast.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building Product Marketing from the ground up, and you'll lead it. This role reports to the CMO. You'll own how Wordsmith tells its story: who we're for, why we win, and how every launch, pitch and campaign lands with in-house legal buyers. At Wordsmith, leaders build. You'll write the positioning and run the first launches yourself, then grow the team around what works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legal AI is noisy. Everyone's making similar claims, and buyers struggle to tell them apart. Underneath the noise is a huge opportunity: in-house legal is one of the last functions without a system built for how it works. That's a new category, and it's wide open. Your job is to define it: what it is, why it matters, and why Wordsmith is the platform in-house teams run on. If you've done that in a fast-moving market and want to build the function that does it, this role is for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own positioning and messaging.</strong> Take our positioning and turn it into the pitch across the sales deck, website and campaigns. Keep one messaging source of truth current as the product and market move.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get in before the build.</strong> Work with Product to define the narrative, the story and the value before teams start building, not when a feature is nearly ready to ship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accelerate how we launch.</strong> Build a clear path from build to ship to launch: launch tiers, one owner for launch comms, and a calendar the business can plan around. Make launches drive adoption and pipeline, not just announcements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Know the buyer better than anyone.</strong> General Counsel, heads of legal, legal ops and the business teams they serve. Run win/loss, sit in on calls, talk to customers, and turn what you learn into sharper messaging and product input.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run competitive.</strong> Build the competitive program reps actually use: battlecards, objection handling and a clear point of view on every alternative a buyer is weighing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equip Sales. </strong>Partner with GTM Enablement so reps can tell the story, handle the hard questions and sell the platform, including pricing and packaging changes as they roll out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feed Growth. </strong>Give Growth, paid, lifecycle and ABM the messaging, offers and content they need to create pipeline globally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build product marketing for the AI era.</strong> Use AI-enabled workflows to run win/loss at scale, synthesize call recordings, test messaging and keep enablement current, so a small team covers more ground.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the team.</strong> Set the hiring bar, hire two product marketers in 2027, and shape how product marketing works alongside Product in an AI-native company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You reason from first principles. You build positioning from what's true about our buyers and market, not from category templates, and you see how messaging, launches, enablement and growth work as one system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built and led product marketing at a B2B software company selling to mid-market and enterprise through a sales-led motion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a builder. You still like doing the work yourself and set the bar by example.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Positioning work that changed how a company sells. You can point to the before and after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp writing and a clear point of view. You can make a complex platform simple without making it generic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial judgment. You tie your work to win rate, sales cycle and pipeline, not output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong cross-functional influence with Product, Sales and executives. You can push back and bring people with you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're AI-forward and fluent in how AI products work. You can go deep with Product and Engineering on agents and models, then explain them to a General Counsel in plain language. You've already rebuilt parts of how you work with AI and can show us.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>It would also be great if you have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Repositioned a product from point solution to platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pricing and packaging work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go-to-market experience across both the US and UK or Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scaled product marketing through Series B and beyond.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we'll measure success</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win rate and sales cycle in competitive deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launches that ship on time and drive adoption and pipeline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rep adoption of the pitch, the deck and competitive materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product marketing team hired, ramped and owning its areas</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you can expect</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of how Wordsmith shows up in the market, as the founding leader of Product Marketing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct partnership with the CMO and close work with the CEO, Product and Sales leaders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The mandate to build the team and the operating model</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and meaningful equity</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong><br />We're an in-office team. We work together because it makes us faster, sharper, and more effective. You should expect to be in the office or out visiting clients as your default.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a high performance environment. We set a high bar, move quickly, and expect people to take ownership of real problems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There isn't always a clear path. The people who do well here figure things out, stay close to the work, and keep pushing until they get to the right outcome.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Wordsmith</strong><br />In-house legal is changing fast, and the companies that define how it works next are being built now. We have the customers, the product momentum and the backing. What we need is the story told so clearly that buyers can't picture running legal any other way. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to build the product marketing function that does that, this is the place.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wordsmith/head-of-product-marketing-london-204404","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795750985},{"slug":"customer-onboarding-and-enablement-lead-edinburgh-59053","company_name":"Wordsmith","title":"Customer Onboarding and Enablement Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Wordsmith</strong><br />Legal touches everything that matters in a business: every deal, every hire, every launch, every risk. Sales runs on Salesforce. Engineering runs on GitHub. In-house legal runs on inboxes, chat threads and tools that weren’t built for it.<br />Wordsmith is changing that. We’re building the platform in-house legal runs on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requests from across the business come in through one front door. AI agents handle the routine work. Lawyers stay in control where judgment matters. Legal finally gets to triage by risk, not by whoever shouted loudest.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re built for in-house teams, not law firms. Our customers want to spend less on outside counsel, not more, and we’re on their side of that equation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">More than 500 companies run on Wordsmith, including Financial Times, Canva, Trip.com, Revolut, Adyen, Trustpilot, and Sage. We’ve raised $100M from Index Ventures, General Catalyst, Highland Europe and others, and we’re growing fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring an Enablement Lead to own how customers learn Wordsmith, and how they become confident, self-sufficient users of it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own onboarding, training and enablement end to end: Legal AI fundamentals, product and feature overviews, self-paced certifications, and re-enablement for customers who've stalled. You'll teach both ends of the customer organisation: the lawyers and business users in Wordsmith every day, and the champions and admins who support their colleagues.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an enablement role, not a delivery or commercial one. You won't own implementation, technical support, renewals, account growth or a sales quota. Your focus is capability: do customers know how to use Wordsmith well, and can they keep learning without us?<br /></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own customer onboarding.</strong> Design and run the journey that takes a newly implemented customer to a confident, capable team, and keep improving it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Teach Legal AI fundamentals.</strong> Build the curriculum that helps legal teams understand what AI agents do well, where judgement stays with them, and how to work alongside the technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run live training.</strong> Lead onboarding sessions, product walkthroughs and feature deep dives for lawyers, business users and admins of every technical confidence level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the self-paced academy.</strong> Create online certifications and learning paths so customers can train new joiners and refresh skills on their own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain the enablement library.</strong> Keep guides and product overviews accurate as Wordsmith ships, and retire what's out of date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Re-enable struggling customers.</strong> Diagnose why adoption has stalled and run focused programmes that get teams back to self-sufficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Train the champions.</strong> Equip customer champions and admins to teach their own colleagues, so capability compounds inside each account.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape in-app help.</strong> Work with Product to build guidance, walkthroughs and prompts into Wordsmith itself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure whether learning worked.</strong> Define what a trained, self-sufficient customer looks like, track it, and use the evidence to change what we teach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner across customer teams.</strong> Work with Transformation, Customer Success, Support Engineering and Product so enablement reflects real implementations, questions and product changes.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–5 years in customer enablement, training, onboarding, customer education, implementation or a similar customer-facing role where teaching was central.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You design learning, not just deliver it. You can turn a complex product into a curriculum with a clear sequence and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence in front of a room, in person and on video, with senior lawyers as readily as with day-to-day users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building self-paced content (courses, certifications, guides, video) and a view on what makes people finish it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear, warm communication style that makes unfamiliar ideas easy to grasp without oversimplifying them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisation: you can run several programmes, sessions and content deadlines at once without losing detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with data. You can read product-usage information, spot where learning hasn't landed and act on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about AI and legal technology. You don't need a legal background, but you'll want to learn the product and our customers' work deeply.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong learning mindset: you welcome feedback, apply coaching and want to grow quickly.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>How we work</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're an hybrid team in Edinburgh or London, so expect to work from the office or visit customers by default. We set a high bar, move quickly and give people real ownership. There won't always be a playbook, so you'll bring curiosity, structure and persistence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with the VP of Transformation and with Customer Success, Account Management and Product. Each customer team has a clear remit:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transformation</strong> leads implementation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support Engineering</strong> resolves technical issues</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Account Management</strong> owns renewals and commercial growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Success</strong> owns adoption, customer health and value realisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enablement</strong> owns onboarding, training and customer capability<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Why join Wordsmith</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wordsmith is growing quickly, winning new customers and expanding inside larger organisations. Because Legal AI is new to almost everyone who buys it, teaching it well is one of the highest-leverage things we can do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join early enough to define wha