:false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wordsmith/events-associate-london-400506","tags":["G&A"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795750985},{"slug":"senior-manager-ceo-office-ma-london-149410","company_name":"bunch","title":"Senior Manager CEO Office - M&A","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.bunch.capital/"><u>bunch</u></a> is building the backbone of private markets. We are enabling next-gen fund operations with one integrated system that combines secure data infrastructure, AI-powered workflows and expert fund services. If you value ownership, growth through real responsibility, and working with a thoughtful, ambitious team, this role might be for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a senior member of the Founders' Office at bunch, you will take the company's highest-priority projects from "we need to do this" to done, owning cross-functional initiatives end-to-end.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead high-importance, high-urgency strategic projects end-to-end — defining the problem, coordinating stakeholders (including senior leadership), running the analysis yourself, and driving projects to completion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take charge of initiatives that cut across departments, stepping into commercial, product, or operations as needed to ensure alignment and delivery of outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct opportunity assessments to provide recommendations that support the Founders in identifying new areas for growth and evaluating new markets, business lines, and products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depending on scale, run one large project with multiple workstreams or several projects in parallel</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify what the company should work on next and make it happen</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–5 years of experience in high-velocity environments (top-tier strategy consulting, investment banking, or a high-growth VC-backed startup), ideally with hands-on startup experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independent and proactive — you identify what needs to happen and move it forward without waiting for direction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to bring the right people in early, build alignment across functions and with senior stakeholders without needing authority, and manage multiple workstreams without dropping balls</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and critical thinking skills — able to break down ambiguous problems, identify root causes, and turn data into actionable insights</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experienced in designing and executing analyses end-to-end, QA'ing your own work rigorously, and delivering outputs that drive decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structures recommendations with a clear "so what" — quantifies trade-offs, flags risks, and proposes a preferred path</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable pushing back on work that doesn't serve the company's top priorities, including your own</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about new tools and quick to adopt what makes you faster — AI-assisted research, drafting, and analysis — while understanding their limits and building your own workflows around them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English required; German is a plus</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Workplace &amp; Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"