style="min-height:1.5em">Witness new auditors in practice, document what you observe and give clear feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Calibre’s platform in live audits and show the product team where changes would improve evidence review, reporting or quality checks.</p></li></ul><h1>What we’re looking for</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A current ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Lead Auditor qualification and a recent audit log.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading third-party ISO 27001 certification audits in a certification-body setting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough hands-on understanding of cloud and security infrastructure to assess evidence such as IAM policies, infrastructure configuration and audit logs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear writing and sound audit judgement. You can explain your conclusions to a client’s technical team and defend them in a review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in using AI-assisted tools in audit work and the judgement to verify their output against the underlying evidence.</p></li></ul><h1>How to apply</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://passport.calibre.ac/job"><u>Create your Auditor Passport</u></a> and upload your CV. If you have your Lead Auditor certificate and audit log to hand, please include those too.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: £60K – £75K • 0.1%</p><ul><li> • Base Salary £60K – £75K • 0.1%</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/calibre/iso-27001-auditor-london-294439","tags":["Certification"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795740015},{"slug":"account-executive-london-385423","company_name":"Ryftpay","title":"Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Ryft</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ryft is a regulated payment facilitator and authorised payment institution building the infrastructure layer for modern commerce platforms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We enable marketplaces, SaaS platforms and multi-party ecosystems to embed and monetise payments natively. Our technology handles onboarding, compliance, orchestration, split payments and revenue sharing, allowing our partners to focus on growth while we manage complexity.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are now entering the next phase of scale, expanding into new verticals and building a category-defining embedded payments platform.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong><br />You’ll own the full sales cycle, from finding and qualifying the right businesses through to negotiating and closing. You’ll sell to founders, CFOs and Heads of Payments, often replacing an incumbent provider they’ve used for years. That means a consultative, technical sale with 3–6 month cycles and multiple stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You’ll have a book of ICP leads to work from, but the best people here build their own pipeline too. You’ll report to a Sales Team Lead and have real autonomy over how you hit your number.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generate and qualify your own pipeline, alongside a book of ICP leads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run discovery to understand how a prospect’s money flows, then shape a solution around it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pitch and demo Ryft to C-suite and senior finance and product stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate commercials (pricing, volumes, contract terms) and close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Solutions, Product, Onboarding and Risk so new clients go live smoothly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep your CRM sharp and forecast accurately</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed what you hear in the market back into product and go-to-market as we enter new regions</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in a closing AE role, ideally selling payments, fintech or financial infrastructure B2B</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of closing complex deals with 3+ month cycles and multiple decision-makers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of building your own pipeline, not just working inbound</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable talking about interchange, acquiring, settlement and pricing models, or able to get there fast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercially sharp: you understand margin, volume and how to structure a deal that works for both sides</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Disciplined CRM habits and accurate forecasting</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling to marketplaces, platforms or SaaS businesses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience displacing incumbent PSPs (Stripe, Adyen, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to European or US markets</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ryftpay/account-executive-london-385423","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795740015},{"slug":"principal-engineer-london-237388","company_name":"Motorway","title":"Principal Engineer","description":"<h1><strong>About Motorway</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motorway is the UK's largest online car-selling platform. We connect private sellers directly with over 8,000 dealers nationwide. Our online platform helps sellers achieve great prices for their cars while giving dealers fast, reliable access to the stock they want for their dealerships. Founded in 2017, our award-winning, technology-led approach has redefined the experience of selling a car. Motorway is backed by some of the world’s leading technology investors, having raised £143 million in Series C funding.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a unique opportunity to join a fast-growing scale-up at a crucial phase of growth and help change an industry for the better.</p><h2><strong>About the team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, I'm Mariot, I lead Engineering here at Motorway. We're around 70 engineers across product teams, building the marketplace and all services around that handles hundreds of vehicle transactions every day. We care about delivering value to the business, getting the architecture engineering sound, keeping the production bar high, and being early and deliberate about the technology we adopt. <br /><br />We have been early adopters of GenAI for software engineering, we've built a reputation for that, and we'd like to keep earning it. AI is enabling us to deliver faster at a much higher quality software while easing the maintenance of our existing services.</p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Principal Engineer to set technical direction and evolve engineering practices  across Motorway, reporting to the Director of Engineering. This is a broad role: your remit spans multiple product areas and every engineering specialties, and your decisions will shape what we build, what we buy, and what we retire.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work with engineering leadership, product, and other functions stakeholders to continuously evolve our overall architecture and practices, and with our senior and staff engineers to turn that direction into working software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own our relationships with AWS on the engineering side, our main cloud provider. It's the foundation of our platform and one of our most important partnerships. In practice, we expect you to lead the following activities:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frequently meet AWS representatives getting access to latest services and features,  share feedback on our usage and needs, and be an early tester and adopter of new services/</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify new services we could adopt to continuously improve our reliability and ability to build new services and features at pace for the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share internally good practices on software engineering at the edge and usage of AWS services, including continuously updating technical recommendations for humans and agents.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> You'll represent Motorway on stage at external events and in the wider engineering community, and you'll set the standard for how engineers here present their work internally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also lead on our adoption of AI for software engineering. We give engineers access to the latest models through Kiro, and we want someone who can define what good looks like when domain depth, AI-enabled breadth, and rigorous evaluation all have to work together.</p><h2><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set technical strategy across multiple product areas, and make the 