ision-statement-725a7e2f659b"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a>)<em> - </em>Every Qontoer gets unlimited access to the best AI tools. We want people who experiment without waiting for permission, push AI beyond the obvious, know when to trust it, and when to question it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us as <strong>Engineering Manager – Accounting Product</strong> and help build the last missing piece of Qonto’s all-in-one offer for businesses. You’ll lead a cross-functional team of engineers making accounting effortless for business owners, under the guidance of Yanis, our Head of Engineering for the Accounting domain.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead your team:</strong> You’ll manage engineers across the stack and help each of them grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put accounting on autopilot:</strong> You’ll build features that generate bookkeeping automatically and show customers, in real time, the VAT they owe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make accounting simple:</strong> You’ll turn complex accounting and tax steps into a clear experience that business owners can complete with confidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring AI into accounting:</strong> You’ll ship AI-first experiences, like a chat that answers customers from their own accounting file.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-own the product:</strong> You’ll shape the roadmap with your Product Manager and Designer, from discovery to impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unblock your team technically:</strong> You’ll dive into design, code reviews and debugging with your engineers, whatever the stack.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People leadership:</strong> You’ve led engineers as a manager or Tech Lead, and you’re driven by helping people grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on technical background:</strong> You’ve built production systems yourself and can help your team solve technical problems in any stack, using AI to get up to speed on languages you know less.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-driven development:</strong> You use AI in your own engineering work and push your team to raise the bar with it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> You’re fluent in English (French is a bonus).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong> You’re familiar with the French accounting world, its services and how accountants work with businesses.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we can offer you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A product at launch:</strong> You’ll join right after the first launch of Qonto Accounting and shape what it becomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visible business impact:</strong> Accounting keeps customers with Qonto for the long run, so your team’s work shows up directly in loyalty.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A domain on the move:</strong> Qonto Accounting is growing fast in France and starting to expand to other European markets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Your future manager</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll report to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yanishammada/">Yanis</a>, Head of Engineering, but don’t expect micro-management. Yanis grew from Lead Engineer to Head of Engineering over 4 years at Qonto. He’s a pragmatic generalist who has built payment integrations from scratch and is as comfortable on the frontend as on the backend. He gives engineers real ownership, values sharing failures as much as wins, and gets out of the way so the team can ship.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Our stack &amp; practices</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our primary languages are <strong>Go</strong> and <strong>Ruby</strong>, <strong>React</strong> for frontend, and <strong>Kotlin</strong> and <strong>Swift</strong> for our mobile apps. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our platform runs on <strong>Kubernetes</strong>, hosted on <strong>AWS</strong>, with <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> as our database of choice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use <strong>Kafka</strong> for event-driven architecture and <strong>ELK</strong> for logging and auditing, among many other tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Each engineer gets access to AI-first tooling (<strong>Claude Code</strong>, <strong>Cursor</strong>, <strong>Notion AI</strong>), and we want people who use AI to raise the bar, not just to go faster. Read our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/ai-at-qonto-vision-statement-725a7e2f659b"><strong>AI vision statement</strong></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use <strong>Linear</strong> as an issue tracking and project management platform for our software development.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Our methodology: the Qonto Way</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value upfront technical design, team code reviews, and smart slicing — quality drives the velocity our customers need.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our lean toolbox, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/qonto-way-strong-engineering-culture-prt1-kaizen-spirit-7e6e0a17c07e">Kaizen</a> and PDCA, lets you drive continuous improvement with your peers and manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to go further? Read about the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/tagged/the-qonto-way">Qonto Way</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ About our hiring process</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2 interviews (1 hour each):</strong> first with your Talent Acquisition Manager, then with Yanis, your future direct manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Live skill test (about 2 hours) with two engineers:</strong> product discussion, system design and an AI-assisted code review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final interview (1 hour):</strong> with Carl, our VP Engineering.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>[DIVERSITY]</strong> <em>At Qonto, we understand that true diversity isn’t just about ticking boxes on a hiring checklist. Apply regardless of the boxes you tick - who knows? You may have the missing piece of the puzzle we’ve been searching for all along.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[HIRING PROCESS DURATION]</strong> <em>On average, <strong>our hiring process lasts 20 working days. </strong>More information on our candidate journey </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/careers/candidate-journey"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[DATA RETENTION]</strong> <em>By applying, you agree that Qonto processes your personal data to assess your application. Your data is kept for up to 2 years in our candidate pool. Read our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/legal-documents/privacy-notice"><em><u>Privacy Notice</u></em></a><em> for full details.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔒 Your security matters to us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment scams are on the rise. Qonto will never work with third-party platforms or agencies that request payment from candidates. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Qonto, please report it to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/qonto/software-engineering-manager-accounting-product-paris-16775","tags":["Tech & Data"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1795686016},{"slug":"gtm-value-creation-lead-paris-326164","company_name":"Hexa","title":"GTM & Value Creation Lead","description":"<h2>About Hexa</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hexa builds and scales software companies alongside entrepreneurs. Since its launch as eFounders, Hexa has helped create companies including Aircall, Spendesk, Front, Swan and Yousign.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hexa Scale is a small-cap software investment firm deploying a €100 million fund. We take majority stakes in established B2B software companies and work directly with their founders to unlock their next stage of growth. We bring capital, but first and formemost operators who get involved in the daily work to build the fundamentals required to ignite a real Sscaling story: go-to-market, product, hiring and the systems needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Hexa Scale</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Many software companies have a strong product and loyal customers but have yet to build a repeatable growth engine. Their next phase calls for more than optimising today’s funnel: they need to rethink how they find, win, serve and grow customers as AI changes both customer workflows and commercial execution. They need people who can test what works with their teams and turn the learning into a way of operating.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That is what we do at Hexa Scale. We invest in software companies with roughly €2–10 million in ARR and work alongside their founders after the investment. Our approach is hands-on, with go-to-market at the centre of the acceleration plan?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Mission</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Value Creation Manager with a strong GTM background to join the Hexa Scale team. You will assess growth opportunities and feasibility before an investment decision, then work across our portfolio with founders and their teams to remove growth bottlenecks. Your judgement will help the investment team test whether a company has strong, executable growth potential; your operating work will help turn that potential into results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a GTM-major role: your core craft is building a next-generation go-to-market engine, combining customer insight, commercial execution, data and AI-enabled workflows. You have built or improved commercial motions inside a fast-growing startup, and you are as comfortable with positioning and customer interviews as with sales execution, pricing &amp; process optimization. The remit can become broader as the needs and maturity of each portfolio company change, particularly where product is the best route to more customer value and growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will not be an external advisor producing slides for a management team. You will work with that team, from within the company, establish a useful operating cadence and leave behind a system they can run without you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a preliminary note and as you’ll understand based on the 4 pillars below, the role is in close synch with the investment team. You’ll be a sparing partner, brining both your expert judgement as well as your field working competences to the table. While the role will enable lots of autonomy, you’ll be working in close synch with one or more investment partners, who’re experienced entrepreneurs you’ll learn from and who’ll have the final call on major decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Participate in investment selection</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Assess growth potential:</strong> Work with the deal team before an investment decision to test whether the growth opportunity is substantial, accessible and actionable, rather than relying on an optimistic management plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support commercial diligence:</strong> support the investment team in interviews of customers and prospects; examine segmentation, win/loss, funnel conversion, sales cycles, retention and expansion, pricing, channels and the capacity of the current team to execute.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Underwrite the growth levers:</strong> Prioritize potential improvements in GTM, pricing, upmarket sales or distribution. Quantify the starting point, expected impact, costs, timing, dependencies and downside. Separate demonstrated opportunities from assumptions that still need testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn diligence into a plan:</strong> Present an evidence-based growth-engineering assessment to the investment team, including what could disprove the thesis and an initial post-close step-by-step execution roadmap. Final investment decisions remain with the partners.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Build a next-generation go-to-market engine</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find the constraint:</strong> Work with founders and commercial teams to understand where growth stalls, from targeting and lead generation to conversion, onboarding and expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get close to customers:</strong> Run interviews, listen to sales calls, examine lost deals and translate what you learn into sharper segmentation, messaging and offers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run experiments:</strong> Lead and co-run tests with teams across outbound, partnerships, demand generation, pricing, AI-assisted prospecting and sales processes. Set a baseline, define what success looks like, measure conversion and unit economics, and stop what doesn’t work, while bringing teams along so the new ways of working stick.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build AI-enabled GTM workflows:</strong> Design and test practical workflows for research, targeting, qualification, sales preparation, customer success or expansion using AI tools and agents where appropriate. Measure quality, adoption, cost and human oversight, not just activity or demos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make the funnel usable:</strong> Improve CRM discipline, pipeline visibility, forecasting and the handoffs between marketing, sales and customer success. Automate repeatable work where it improves the customer experience and commercial outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Execute alongside portfolio teams</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Connect product and growth:</strong> As portfolio needs and maturity vary, partner with product teams to increase customer value and create new growth paths. Explore features such as embedded finance or agentic execution where relevant; validate customer demand, adoption, willingness to pay, implementation costs and margins before treating them as growth levers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work with founders:</strong> Help turn priorities into a weekly cadence, clear owners and decisions grounded in customer and commercial evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build internal capability:</strong> Coach or assist in recruiting when needed the people who will own the work long term. Document the useful parts of a playbook without imposing the same answer on every company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own critical projects:</strong> Take responsibility for a defined growth or operating problem, from diagnosis through implementation, rather than handing over a recommendation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Can include temporary embedding in the company on a full-time basis</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Strengthen the Hexa Scale operating model</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make our work repeatable:</strong> Capture what works across portfolio companies and improve the tools and methods we use to diagnose and accelerate growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take on adjacent problems:</strong> GTM remains your major, but the most valuable work may extend into product, customer operations, hiring or cross-functional execution depending on the company and its stage of maturity. Know when to take ownership and when to bring in a specialist.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Use technology pragmatically:</strong> Build and deploy AI-enabled workflows with portfolio teams when they improve GTM outcomes or customer value. Assess reliability, cost and operational fit; do not confuse a demo with an adopted process.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we’re looking for</h2><h3>Experience</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Five years or more:</strong> Substantial time in a fast-growing startup or scale-up in a hands-on GTM role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial execution:</strong> You have personally built, operated or significantly improved a B2B growth engine, ideally in a fast-growing startup. You can explain how you changed the GTM motion, what the numbers showed and what you would do differently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>B2B software:</strong> You understand sales cycles, conversion, retention, expansion, pricing and the trade-offs involved in scaling a team. Experience in high growth vertical SaaS is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Range:</strong> You can work across sales, marketing, customer success and operations without needing a large team or a perfectly defined brief.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working with leaders:</strong> Experience alongside founders or senior commercial leaders is a strong plus. French and English fluency are required for this role.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Mindset</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomous:</strong> You can turn an ambiguous problem into a plan, make progress and know when a decision needs to be escalated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on:</strong> You are willing to inspect the CRM, join customer calls, rewrite a sequence and run an experiment yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-fluent:</strong> You already build with AI tools and use them in your daily work, not just in occasional demos. You can show workflows or products you have built, explain what worked and failed, and help teams adopt AI where it changes how they go to market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercially sharp:</strong> You care about revenue outcomes, not activity for its own sake.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Versatile without being superficial:</strong> GTM is your major, but you can work on product and wider operating problems when they are the real constraint. You connect new customer value to adoption, pricing, retention and growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low ego, high standards:</strong> You can challenge a founder’s assumption, listen when you are wrong and earn the trust of the team doing the work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> A role at the centre of Hexa Scale’s work with founders, with responsibility for real operating projects across B2B software companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team:</strong> Direct collaboration with Hexa Scale partners and access to Hexa’s product, talent, brand and operational expertise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation:</strong> A competitive package, including carried interest</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong> Hexa employee benefits may include a Swile meal card, RTT, a green mobility budget and health insurance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Recruitment process</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proposed process, to confirm with the Talent team:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductory call with Hexa’s Talent team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with the Hexa Scale team on your GTM experience and operating approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical case on a real pre-investment growth diligence and portfolio execution problem, followed by a working session.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conversations with the people you would work with most closely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reference checks and offer.</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/hexa/gtm-value-creation-lead-paris-326164","tags":["Hexa"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795686013},{"slug":"auditeur-preleveur-h-f-en-restauration-collective-quimper-220547","company_name":"IFBM et Qualtech Groupe","title":"Auditeur préleveur (H/F) en restauration collective","description":"<p>Le Groupe QUALTECH - 5 sociétés, 7 sites et 350 salariés - est un regroupement de Laboratoires spécialisés dans les analyses de laboratoire (microbiologie, biologie moléculaire, chimie, extraction d’ADN, etc), le conseil, la recherche et la formation. Notre but est de garantir une expertise qualitative à nos clients en termes de contrôle, de qualité et de fiabilité dans le secteur de l’agro-alimentaire.</p><p>Nos valeurs : intégrité, innovation, expertise, engagement, orientation client. En rejoignant son laboratoire AGROBIO spécialisé en microbiologie, vous participez à son expertise dans le monde de la recherche et de l’analyse agro-alimentaire.</p><h2>Vos missions</h2><p>Dans le cadre d’un remplacement au sein de notre laboratoire AGROBIO, nous vous attendons pour prélever des échantillons (alimentaires, d’eau et de surface) et réaliser des audits d’hygiène chez nos clients situés dans un rayon de 120 km autour de Quimper.</p><p>Vous allez avoir l’opportunité de rencontrer les différents acteurs locaux et de découvrir leur activité, qu’ils soient spécialisés dans la restauration collective (crèches, lycées, maisons de retraite, restaurants d’entreprise, armé, abattoirs, etc.) ou plus traditionnelle.</p><p>Vous êtes le 1er maillon de cette longue chaîne menant à une analyse de haute fiabilité grâce à la collaboration de chacun. Derrière vous, une équipe logistique présente à tout moment pour vous aider, des techniciens de laboratoire impatients de traiter vos échantillons et des clients à rassurer sur leurs bonnes pratiques vis-à-vis du grand public. Des outils de travail vous sont attribués : un véhicule de service, une carte carburant et de télépéage, un téléphone, une tablette, et des paniers repas pour chaque journée de travail de plus de 6 heures. Enfin, une formation sera assurée en interne à votre prise de poste.</p><p>La connaissance de la méthode HACCP sera considérée comme un atout dans votre can