<li><p><span style="color:#121317">Mehrjährige CAD-Erfahrung, vorzugsweise Siemens NX</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Erfahrung in der Entwicklung von Werkzeugmaschinen wünschenswert</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Logisches Denken, Kreativität, Teamfähigkeit und Belastbarkeit</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Auszug aus den Benefits von unserem Kunden</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Klare Strategie und Ziele<br></span></strong><span style="color:#121317">„Wir sind ein Nachhaltigkeits- und Innovationspionier mit einem besonderen Mehrwert für unsere Kunden“ ist unsere Vision und davon lassen wir uns leiten.<br></span></p><p class="mb_s12 lastOfType:mb_s0 textStyle_body2" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Fokus auf Nachhaltigkeit und Innovation<br></span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Wir haben hohe Nachhaltigkeits- und Innovationsziele. Lassen Sie uns gemeinsam auf eine nachhaltige Zukunft hinarbeiten.<br></span></p><p class="mb_s12 lastOfType:mb_s0 textStyle_body2" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Ausgezeichnete Schulungsinstrumente<br></span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Wir bieten Entwicklungsmöglichkeiten für alle. Wir bieten globale Lerntools sowie Schulungen und spezialisierte Kurse.<br></span></p><p class="mb_s12 lastOfType:mb_s0 textStyle_body2" style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Ausgezeichnete Karrierechancen<br></span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Als global agierendes Unternehmen bieten wir viele Möglichkeiten zur Karriereentwicklung. Wir bieten einen Talentmanagementprozess, um Ihre Karriere zu fördern.</span></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/cross-ing-ag/ingenieurin-maschinenbau-80-100-langnau-im-emmental-126245","tags":["Langnau im Emmental"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Langnau im Emmental, Bern, Schweiz","created_at":1795566696},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-zurich-391423","company_name":"sizeless","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","description":"<p>sizeless builds the data layer for physical AI in construction. Contractors film an open trench with a smartphone. Our system turns that video into a 3D model, recognises what is in the ground, and delivers the documentation the industry needs – CAD, BIM, GIS and quantities. The same data is the foundation for training the robots that will one day work on construction sites.</p><p>It is a real problem with real customers: construction and utilities still document reality by hand, and almost nothing about that process has changed in decades. We are a small team with research experience from ETH Zurich, UC Berkeley and MIT, and we are looking for an engineer who wants to bring this technology onto real construction sites and make it work for our customers.</p><h2>Tasks</h2><ul><li><p>Work directly with our customers – contractors, utilities and surveyors in Switzerland, Germany and Austria – from first site visit to daily use</p></li><li><p>Get field crews up and running with our capture app, on site and remotely</p></li><li><p>Adapt our outputs to each customer's CAD, GIS and documentation standards</p></li><li><p>Write the scripts, integrations and tooling that connect sizeless to customer systems</p></li><li><p>Bring what you learn on site back into the product, together with the engineering team</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>Solid engineering fundamentals in TypeScript, Python or a comparable language</p></li><li><p>You enjoy working with customers and are comfortable on a construction site</p></li><li><p>Ownership: you take problems personally and see them through</p></li><li><p>Fluent German and English – most of our customers work in German</p></li><li><p>Willingness to travel regularly within Switzerland, Germany and Austria and valid driving licence (category B)</p></li></ul><p>Experience with 3D data, mobile apps or geospatial systems is welcome. We care more that you learn quickly and take details seriously.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Early team member with real ownership – your work ships to paying customers, not a demo</p></li><li><p>Employee stock options: you own part of what you build</p></li><li><p>New office in Zürich Kreis 5</p></li><li><p>Modern, AI-first toolchain – we invest in whatever makes you faster</p></li><li><p>Work directly with the founders</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/sizeless/forward-deployed-engineer-zurich-391423","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1795573047},{"slug":"senior-research-scientist-3d-reconstruction-spatial-ai-zurich-143119","company_name":"intrinsicrobotics","title":"Senior Research Scientist 3D Reconstruction & Spatial AI","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Intrinsic is an AI robotics group at Google aiming to reimagine the potential of industrial robotics. Our team believes that advances in AI, perception and simulation will redefine what’s possible for industrial robotics in the near future – with software and data at the core.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make industrial robotics intelligent, accessible, and usable for millions more businesses, entrepreneurs, and developers. We are a dynamic team of engineers, roboticists, designers, and technologists who are passionate about unlocking the creative and economic potential of industrial robotics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior 3D Reconstruction &amp;amp; Spatial AI Engineer, you will own the development of the geometric and semantic perception stacks that power our physical AI framework. You will design real-time systems that enable our robots to translate unstructured, dynamic 3D environments into structured, queryable world models - seamlessly linking high-level task planners (such as VLM/VLA models) directly to robust, low-level manipulation and grasp policies in Flowstate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How your work moves the mission forward&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy real-time spatial perception and state estimation pipelines using both in-house models like Gemini/Gemma and open source models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build multi-sensor fusion pipelines integrating RGB-D, stereo cameras, and IMU data into dense spatial representations (ex: point clouds, neural occupancy grids, or implicit signed distance function fields)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ground high-level semantic concepts into 3D geometric structures. This means building queryable, object-centric 3D scene graphs that map not just where an object is, but what it is, and its relationship to the other objects, and its functional properties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate open-vocabulary vision language models (ex: CLiP based visual descriptors, DINOv2) into 3D metric space to allow the robot to reason about natural language instructions (ex: ‘pick up the half-eaten apple and put it in the trash bin’)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop learning-based spatial models (such as 3D Diffusion Policies) that utilize 3D point clouds to predict continuous grasp poses and trajectories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate abstract semantic logic into functional affordances (ex: identifying the ‘graspable’ part of a mug versus the ‘containment’ part)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with eng teams to ensure that stochastic, learned semantic models cleanly map to deterministic safe boundaries on physical hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive data strategies for collecting, labeling, and generating 3D synthetic data&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Skills you will need to be successful&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; PhD (preferred) or Master’s in Robotics, Computer Vision, Machine Learning, or a related quantitative field—with a focus on Spatial AI, SLAM, or Embodied AI .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3D Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep mathematical foundations in multi-view geometry, camera calibration, visual-inertial odometry (VIO), and probabilistic state estimation .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern Deep Learning:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience training and deploying multimodal architectures (VLMs/VLAs), contrastive learning frameworks, or 3D neural scene representations (NeRFs, Gaussian Splatting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming &amp;amp; Systems&lt;/strong&gt;: Expert level command of Python (PyTorch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Skills that will differentiate your candidacy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with robotics middleware (ROS2) and real time execution constraints would be a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on &quot;battle scars&quot; from deploying onto physical robotic manipulators or mobile platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Intrinsic, we are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. Employment at Intrinsic is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications directly related to professional competence. Intrinsic does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. It is Intrinsic’s policy to comply with all applicable national, state and local laws pertaining to nondiscrimination and equal opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please contact us at: -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/intrinsicrobotics/senior-research-scientist-3d-reconstruction-spatial-ai-zurich-143119","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1795557316},{"slug":"technical-project-manager-zurich-363655","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Technical Project Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work on our most strategic accounts and turn signed deals into live, revenue-generating deployments. On our largest global rollouts, successfully embedding BLP in the customer's system landscape (e.g., ERP) decides whether the go-live date holds. As a Technical Project Manager, you own the technical solution. You shape it with the customer's enterprise architects and IT leads, write the specification our engineers build from, and drive internal alignment and on-time delivery.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the technical solution with the customer’s business and IT departments on large and complex accounts, and push until answers are specific enough to build on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn requirements into a clear, implementable specification for our engineers. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage external and internal technical stakeholders, ensuring timely delivery and aligned priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flag major development needs and blockers early, and bring a clear recommendation to the customer's steering committee.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Project Managers on technical feasibility, effort and sequencing, through the first go-live.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years in solution design, technical consulting, enterprise integration or technical product work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of delivering complex technical projects from requirements engineering to go-live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing specifications that engineers can build from without a translation layer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of how enterprise systems exchange data, from file-based interfaces to APIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, spoken and written.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of purchase-to-pay (P2P) and order-to-cash (O2C) processes, including the related finance and accounting workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading the technical design on multi-ERP and multi-country projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on knowledge of several ERP systems (e.g., SAP, Microsoft Dynamics, Oracle, Infor), from both a functional and an integration perspective.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why BLP</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fast-growing, global AI company: the ideal place to learn and accelerate your career.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of the technical design on our largest, most complex customer programs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one month of onboarding at our Zurich headquarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee ownership through our participation program.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Practical information</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: our Munich or Cologne office (hybrid with 3+ office days per week)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel: up to 10%, mostly within DACH</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employment: full-time, permanent</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/technical-project-manager-zurich-363655","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1795556416},{"slug":"senior-marketer-ai-expert-remote-emea-switzerland-436216","company_name":"Weekday 1","title":"Senior Marketer, AI Expert (Remote, EMEA)","description":"<p><strong>This role is for one of our clients</strong></p><p><strong>Compensation: $60 - $85 per hour</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Remote – United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland<br><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ Years<br><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full-Time<br><strong>Work Commitment:</strong> Approximately 40 Hours per Week<br><strong>Compensation:</strong> Based on Location and Experience</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p>We are looking for experienced Senior Marketing Professionals to join the in-house marketing team of a leading AI-focused organization. This is an opportunity to contribute directly to marketing strategy, execution, and growth initiatives within a technology-driven environment.</p><p>You will take ownership of a primary marketing discipline aligned with your expertise, such as Product Marketing, Demand Generation, Growth Marketing, Lifecycle Marketing, Brand Marketing, Communications, or Field Marketing.</p><p>Working closely with cross-functional teams, you will develop and execute marketing programs, support product launches, and drive regional go-to-market initiatives across EMEA. This is a hands-on functional role suited to experienced marketing professionals who can independently lead strategic programs and influence senior stakeholders.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><p>Depending on your area of specialization, your responsibilities may include:</p><ul><li>Developing product positioning, messaging frameworks, value propositions, and launch strategies for products and features.</li><li>Planning and executing integrated campaigns across demand generation, lifecycle marketing, events, and field marketing.</li><li>Creating, editing, and reviewing marketing content for technical and business audiences.</li><li>Monitoring campaign performance and reporting on pipeline contribution, engagement, conversion, and ROI.</li><li>Collaborating with product, sales, communications, and regional marketing teams to execute go-to-market strategies.</li><li>Adapting global marketing programs to local markets and regional customer requirements.</li><li>Using data-driven insights to improve campaign effectiveness and marketing performance.</li><li>Independently managing strategic marketing initiatives and ensuring successful execution.</li></ul><h2>Core Qualifications</h2><ul><li>7+ years of professional marketing experience, preferably in in-house roles within technology, AI, or B2B SaaS companies.</li><li>Strong expertise in at least one of the following marketing disciplines:</li><ul><li>Product Marketing</li><li>Demand Generation</li><li>Growth Marketing</li><li>Lifecycle Marketing</li><li>Brand Marketing</li><li>Marketing Communications</li><li>Field Marketing</li></ul><li>Proven experience independently owning and delivering significant marketing programs.</li><li>Ability to influence senior stakeholders and collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams.</li><li>Excellent written and verbal communication, content development, and presentation skills.</li><li>Comfortable working with marketing analytics, performance metrics, and tools such as HubSpot, Salesforce, and Google Analytics.</li><li>Ability to work in a fast-paced, technology-focused environment.</li><li>Candidates with exclusively agency-based experience may be less suited to this role.</li></ul><h2>Preferred Candidate Profile</h2><ul><li>Senior marketing professionals with deep expertise in at least one core marketing function.</li><li>Experienced individual contributors who have independently led strategic initiatives; a formal people-management title is not mandatory.</li><li>Professionals with backgrounds in AI, technology, enterprise software, or B2B SaaS.</li><li>Candidates comfortable working with global and regional teams across EMEA.</li></ul><h2>Application Process</h2><ol><li>Submit your updated resume.</li><li>Complete a short screening questionnaire outlining your experience and marketing specialization.</li><li>Participate in a short AI-moderated interview.</li><li>During the interview, select your primary marketing discipline, such as Product Marketing, Demand Generation, or another relevant specialization.</li></ol><p><strong>Working Language:</strong> English for both the role and interview process.</p><h2>Engagement &amp; Compensation</h2><ul><li>Full-time commitment of approximately 40 hours per week.</li><li>Fully remote opportunity open to candidates based in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland.</li><li>The engagement may be structured as an independent contractor arrangement or employment through a local partner, depending on location and applicable requirements.</li><li>Compensation will be determined based on the candidate's location, experience, and expertise and discussed during the screening process.</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/weekday-1/senior-marketer-ai-expert-remote-emea-switzerland-436216","tags":["AI Training","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1795555218},{"slug":"swisschips-connect-recruiting-registration-form-zurich-22730","company_name":"Axelera AI","title":"SwissChips Connect - recruiting registration form","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the page to register your interest in opportunities with Axelera AI following the 23 November, SwissChips Connect event in Zurich.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The deadline to share your information: <strong>30 November, 18:00 CEST</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/axelera-ai/swisschips-connect-recruiting-registration-form-zurich-22730","tags":["Events"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Zurich (on-site)","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"stagiaire-communication-experience-client-carouge-296687","company_name":"AQUA SWIM","title":"Stagiaire Communication & Expérience Client","description":"<h2>À propos d'Aqua Swim Academy</h2><p>Aqua Swim Academy est une école de natation pour enfants et adultes présente autour du Lac Léman, notamment à Genève, Coppet, Lausanne, Montreux et Aubonne. Nous proposons des cours tout au long de l'année ainsi que des camps pendant les vacances scolaires. Notre mission : faire progresser chaque nageur dans l'eau, avec plaisir et en confiance.</p><p>Pour accompagner notre développement, nous recherchons une personne polyvalente qui contribuera à la fois à la communication de notre marque et à l'accueil des familles.</p><h2>Vos missions</h2><h3>Communication & marketing</h3><ul><li><p>Créer des contenus pour nos réseaux sociaux (Instagram, Facebook et LinkedIn) : photos, vidéos et stories.</p></li><li><p>Participer à la préparation de la newsletter et des campagnes d'inscription.</p></li><li><p>Réaliser des reportages et couvrir nos événements : portes ouvertes, camps et compétitions.</p></li><li><p>Suivre les statistiques de communication et proposer des idées pour développer notre communauté.</p></li></ul><h3>Accueil & relation familles</h3><ul><li><p>Accueillir les familles et les nageurs lors des journées de cours et des camps, et veiller à ce que tout se passe bien sur place.</p></li><li><p>Faire le lien entre les familles, les coachs et l'équipe : répondre aux questions, transmettre les retours.</p></li><li><p>Contribuer à une expérience client chaleureuse et soignée, du premier cours aux événements.</p></li></ul><h2>Votre profil</h2><ul><li><p>Vous suivez une formation en communication ou en marketing.</p></li><li><p>Vous êtes à l'aise dans la relation client, accueillant·e, organisé·e et doté·e d'un bon sens du service.</p></li><li><p>Vous êtes créatif·ve et maîtrisez les réseaux sociaux et les outils de création de contenu.</p></li><li><p>Vous avez un niveau de français parfait et un excellent niveau d'anglais. Une autre langue constitue un atout.</p></li><li><p>Vous appréciez le sport et l'univers de la natation.</p></li></ul><h2>Ce que nous vous offrons</h2><ul><li><p>Des responsabilités concrètes et une expérience professionnalisante au quotidien.</p></li><li><p>Une vision globale du fonctionnement d'une entreprise sportive en développement, entre opérations, relation client et marketing.</p></li><li><p>Une équipe jeune, dynamique et internationale.</p></li><li><p>L'opportunité de participer activement à des projets variés et de proposer vos propres idées.</p></li></ul><h2>Conditions du stage</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Lieu :</strong> Genève (Acacias), avec des déplacements ponctuels sur nos différents sites.</p></li><li><p><strong>Début :</strong> dès que possible.</p></li><li><p><strong>Durée :</strong> dès 4 mois.</p></li><li><p><strong>Taux d'activité :</strong> à définir.</p></li><li><p><strong>Convention :</strong> stage conventionné, une convention de stage est obligatoire.</p></li><li><p><strong>Rémunération :</strong> stage non rémunéré.</p></li></ul><p>Envie de rejoindre l'aventure Aqua Swim Academy ? Postulez directement via cette annonce. Nous nous réjouissons de faire votre connaissance !</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/aqua-swim/stagiaire-communication-experience-client-carouge-296687","tags":["Social Media Manager"],"job_types":["Convention de stage (praktikumsvertrag)","internship","aucune expérience requise / Étudiant"],"location":"Carouge","created_at":1795536049},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-geneva-paris-france-332974","company_name":"Proton","title":"Senior Product Manager","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Proton and build a better internet where privacy is the default&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 by scientists who met at CERN, Proton was built on the belief that &lt;strong&gt;privacy is a fundamental human right&lt;/strong&gt;. What started as an encrypted email service has grown into an ecosystem of privacy-first products, including Proton Mail, VPN, Drive, Pass, and Calendar, used by millions of people worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re profitable, independent, and building for the long term. Free from venture capital control and advertising-driven business models, we focus on what matters most: our users. Our work helps protect digital freedom, from everyday privacy to supporting journalists and activists in challenging environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we&#39;re an international team of 700+ people, with offices across 9 countries. We have high standards for the people we hire and the work we do. You&#39;ll work alongside talented, driven colleagues who challenge each other, take ownership, and care about getting things right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explore our &lt;a href=&quot;https://proton.me/community/open-source&quot;&gt;open-source projects&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;Lexical__h3&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;Lexical__paragraph&quot;&gt;We&#39;re building something new at Proton and we&#39;re hiring a Senior PM to lead it from the front.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;Lexical__paragraph&quot;&gt;This role sits at the intersection of product strategy, community dynamics, and Proton&#39;s mission to give people back control over their digital lives. You&#39;ll own the roadmap and execution for a product that brings privacy-first community experiences to millions of users. The team is small and senior; the scope is large. You’ll turn an ambitious product direction into clear strategy, crisp requirements, shipped experiences, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;Lexical__paragraph&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who has lived inside community products: who understands how engagement compounds, why moderation decisions shape culture, and how trust is built (and destroyed) at scale. If you&#39;ve helped build or grow a platform where users interact, organize, and belong, and you want to do it in a way that doesn&#39;t exploit the people using it, this is the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;Lexical__h3&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;Lexical__ul Lexical__ul--depth-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;Lexical__listItem&quot; value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Define and drive the product strategy and roadmap end-to-end — from first principles through to shipped features — without waiting for direction from above&lt;/li&gt;
