ons gain greater visibility, understanding, and control over their data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a fully remote and internationally distributed company, we combine technical excellence with a collaborative and adaptable way of working. Our mission is simple: to help organizations turn information into action, enabling faster, smarter decisions when they matter most.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Finance Controller to own DTACT’s finance function end-to-end as we continue to scale internationally. Reporting into the COO, you’ll take full ownership of accounting, collections, financial analytics, budgeting, and compliance (including our Dutch statutory obligations) — acting as the single point of accountability for finance in the business today. This is a hands-on, mid-level role: you’ll be expected to run the entire finance function largely on your own in the near term, while also bringing the leadership mindset and ambition to grow the function — and your own role — as DTACT expands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own end-to-end accounting operations — AP/AR, general ledger, and month end/year-end close — ensuring accurate, timely financial reporting.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the full collections process: invoicing, aging follow-up, and cash flow forecasting.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain finance analytics (dashboards, reports) that give leadership clear, real-time visibility into company performance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the budgeting and forecasting cycle, partnering with department leads to track actuals against plan.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure full compliance with Dutch tax and statutory reporting requirements (VAT, annual accounts) and manage relationships with external accountants, auditors, banks, and tax advisors.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with People Operations on payroll processing and accuracy across jurisdictions, and own administration of the employee Stock Option Plan (ESOP).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and continuously improve finance processes, technical efficiencies and controls, laying the groundwork as the company grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–8 years of progressive finance/accounting experience, including hands-on ownership of a full finance function — ideally within tech in a startup or scale-up environment.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid knowledge of Dutch accounting standards, tax regulations, statutory compliance requirements and payroll.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to independently manage accounting, collections, budgeting, and financial analytics without a large supporting team.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills and financial modeling ability; comfortable turning data into clear, actionable insights.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership potential and genuine ambition to grow into a finance leadership role as the team and company scale.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on, “roll up your sleeves” attitude, paired with the ability to think and plan strategically.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills in English and Dutch.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What's in for you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation and equity participation</strong>, including an Employee Stock Option Plan (ESOP), allowing you to share in DTACT's long-term success.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first flexibility</strong>, with the opportunity to work from anywhere within compatible time zones and a schedule that supports both collaboration and personal needs.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A trust-based culture built around asynchronous communication</strong>, empowering people to work independently while staying connected and aligned across teams.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous time off</strong>, including vacation days and local public holidays to help you rest, recharge, and maintain a healthy work-life balance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Home office support</strong>, including high-quality equipment and a budget to create a productive and comfortable workspace.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An international and diverse team</strong>, where English is our company language and collaboration spans multiple countries, backgrounds, and perspectives.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-impact work:</strong> DTACT helps organizations in and outside the government with mitigating their vulnerabilities and providing alerts to incoming threats.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We believe diverse teams build better solutions.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>DTACT welcomes applications from all qualified candidates, regardless of background or identity. We hire based on skills, experience, and potential, and encourage everyone who meets the role requirements to apply.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please note: </strong>Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. Candidates must be authorized to work in their country of residence.</em> <br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dtact/finance-controller-anywhere-in-the-netherlands-364874","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Anywhere in the Netherlands","created_at":1795545615},{"slug":"legal-counsel-netherlands-hybrid-300479","company_name":"Axelera AI","title":"Legal Counsel","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Position Overview</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Axelera AI is a fast-growing AI semiconductor company headquartered in Eindhoven, building high-performance, energy-efficient AI acceleration hardware and software, from the Metis AI platform for edge inference to next-generation AI processing units. We are scaling quickly: new customers, new partners, new markets, and a growing volume of complex commercial deals across the global semiconductor supply chain.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced commercial lawyer to be the engine of our commercial legal function. You will close deals, build the playbooks and processes that let the business move fast without taking on unmanaged risk, and lead how legal operates day to day, with AI in the loop so a lean team delivers more with less. This is a hands-on role with real scope to shape the function as it grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Commercial contracting</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft, review and negotiate a high volume of commercial agreements: customer, distribution, reseller and OEM/ODM agreements; sales terms and EULAs; supply and manufacturing agreements (foundry, OSAT, component suppliers); technology and IP licences; software and SaaS agreements; evaluation, early access and development agreements; R&amp;D collaboration and consortium agreements; services and vendor agreements; and MOUs, LOIs and partnership terms.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the trusted, pragmatic adviser to Sales, Product, Engineering, Operations and Finance, giving clear, commercial risk calls at pace.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise on key semiconductor and AI issues: IP ownership and licensing, warranties and liability caps, product liability, export controls and sanctions, data protection and the EU AI Act.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the CFO and Head of Legal on strategic matters, including corporate transactions and board-level work, as needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Playbooks and scale</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-ready contract playbooks, fallback positions and approval matrices so AI tools and the business can handle routine deals with minimal Legal involvement.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and own a library of standard templates for our core agreement types (e.g. NDA, customer terms, evaluation, distributor, supplier) aligned to our risk appetite.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train commercial teams on contract basics, negotiation positions and when to escalate to Legal.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Legal operations</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead legal operations: intake and triage, prioritisation, SLAs and reporting on legal workload and turnaround.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the legal tech and AI stack: select, implement and continuously improve AI review and drafting tools, CLM, e-signature and the contract repository, automating repeatable work end to end.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own contract lifecycle management, including obligation tracking, renewals and keeping contract records complete and up to date.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up clear policies and processes that scale with the company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Collaboration</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work alongside, supervise and mentor a Junior Legal Counsel, allocating work and reviewing output.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage external counsel efficiently, including scope and budget, and determine which matters are best handled in-house.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report to the Head of Legal (in the interim, the CFO) and help shape the future structure of the legal team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Essential</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified lawyer with 7+ years' PQE in commercial and corporate law, from a leading firm and/or in-house.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantial in-house experience in tech, semiconductors, hardware or deep tech, ideally at a scale-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong track record negotiating complex, high-value international contracts, including IP-heavy and supply chain deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on use of AI tools in daily legal work, plus experience building playbooks and processes that let a small team scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial judgement that finds the route to yes, and the ability to explain risk simply to senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguity, high volume and shifting priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent business English, our working and contract language.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Desirable</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Semiconductor, AI or embedded systems experience (foundry, licensing, OEM deals).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of export controls (EU dual-use, US EAR), sanctions and the EU AI Act.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience implementing CLM or AI contract tools, prompting, or building no-code automations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience mentoring junior lawyers, or exposure to venture-backed companies and governance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dutch or another European language.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work: AI-First Legal</strong><br />We're building a lean legal function, not scaling by headcount. AI handles first-pass review, redlining, drafting and research, while lawyers focus on judgement and negotiation. Routine work is self-serve through templates and AI-assisted workflows. We measure turnaround and outcomes, and we use AI responsibly, with human review and clear guardrails on confidentiality and accuracy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong><br />Hybrid, with 2 days per week in our Amsterdam or Eindhoven office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is your chance to shape and be part of a dynamic, fast-growing, international organization. We offer an attractive compensation package, including a pension plan, extensive employee insurances and the option to get company shares.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An open culture that supports creativity and continual innovation is awaiting you. Collaborative ownership and freedom with responsibility is characteristic for the way we act and work as a team. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Axelera AI, we wholeheartedly embrace equal opportunity and hold diversity in the highest regard. Our steadfast commitment is to cultivate a warm and inclusive environment that empowers and celebrates every member of our team. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds to join us in shaping the future of AI.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Axelera AI may at times work with external parties (such as recruiters, headhunters, or executive search firms) to support both publicly posted and confidential searches. Our hiring process never involves any payment from candidates, and we will never require you to use a particular paid service to be considered for a role. If you have been approached by someone on our behalf and want to confirm it’s legitimate, please contact us directly at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="ms-outlook-linkify" ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/axelera-ai/legal-counsel-netherlands-hybrid-300479","tags":["Corporate Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands (hybrid)","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"mainframe-data-engineer-3-to-6-months-contract-amsterdam-446165","company_name":"Belmont Lavan Ltd","title":"Mainframe Data Engineer - 3 to 6 Months Contract","description":"<p>We are seeking an experienced <strong>Senior Data Engineer</strong> with a strong background in designing, deploying, configuring, and managing enterprise-scale data engineering platforms within secure, on-premises and air-gapped environments.</p><p>The ideal candidate will have extensive hands-on experience working with <strong>Apache Hadoop and Apache Spark clusters</strong>, including installation, configuration, administration, troubleshooting, performance optimisation, and workload management in environments with restricted or no internet connectivity.</p><p>This role will support our <strong>Global Data Centre (GDC)</strong> environment, requiring a candidate who understands the operational and technical challenges of delivering robust, scalable, and secure data platforms within isolated infrastructure.</p><p>The successful candidate will work closely with infrastructure, platform, DevOps, and data engineering teams to build and maintain reliable data processing capabilities.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Design, deploy, configure, and maintain Apache Hadoop and Apache Spark clusters in on-premises and air-gapped environments.</li><li>Manage the full lifecycle of Hadoop/Spark platforms, including installation, upgrades, patching, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting.</li><li>Develop, implement, and maintain scalable data pipelines for batch and distributed data processing.</li><li>Optimise Spark workloads and Hadoop cluster performance, including resource allocation, job scheduling, and capacity management.</li><li>Work with PostgreSQL and other enterprise data systems to support data integration, storage, and processing requirements.</li><li>Support the deployment and management of containerised applications using Kubernetes and Helm.</li><li>Implement and manage service-to-service communication and traffic management using Istio Service Mesh.</li><li>Ensure software dependencies, container images, packages, and platform components can be deployed and maintained without external internet connectivity.</li><li>Implement secure configuration and operational practices aligned with enterprise security requirements.</li><li>Troubleshoot complex infrastructure, cluster, application, and data pipeline issues.</li><li>Collaborate with infrastructure, security, DevOps, and application teams to ensure platform stability and availability.</li><li>Maintain technical documentation, deployment procedures, operational runbooks, and platform architecture documentation.</li><li>Support integration with legacy enterprise data systems, including VSAM.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h2>Required Technical Skills &amp; Experience</h2><p><strong>1. Apache Hadoop &amp; Apache Spark</strong></p><ul><li>Strong hands-on experience deploying, configuring, and administering Apache Hadoop clusters.</li><li>Proven experience deploying and managing Apache Spark clusters and workloads.</li><li>Experience with distributed data processing, batch processing, and large-scale data pipelines.</li><li>Strong understanding of cluster architecture, resource management, performance tuning, and troubleshooting.</li><li>Experience operating big data platforms in on-premises and air-gapped environments.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Air-Gapped &amp; On-Premises Infrastructure</strong></p><ul><li>Practical experience working in isolated, restricted-network, or air-gapped environments.</li><li>Understanding of offline software installation, dependency management, package repositories, and container image management.</li><li>Experience managing platform deployments without direct access to public internet repositories.</li><li>Knowledge of secure infrastructure operations and enterprise deployment standards.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Containerisation &amp; Platform Engineering</strong></p><ul><li>Experience with Kubernetes-based platform deployments.</li><li>Hands-on experience with Helm charts for application and platform deployments.</li><li>Working knowledge of Istio Service Mesh, including traffic management, service discovery, and secure service-to-service communication.</li><li>Understanding of container orchestration and microservices architecture.</li></ul><p><strong>4. Data Systems &amp; Engineering</strong></p><ul><li>Strong experience with PostgreSQL, including database integration and performance considerations.</li><li>Experience designing, developing, and maintaining data pipelines.</li><li>Understanding of distributed data storage and processing architectures.</li><li>Knowledge of VSAM and integration with legacy enterprise data environments.</li></ul><h2>Preferred / Desirable Skills</h2><ul><li>Experience supporting large-scale enterprise or government data centre environments.</li><li>Familiarity with Linux system administration.</li><li>Experience with infrastructure automation and configuration management.</li><li>Knowledge of data security, access controls, encryption, and secure data handling.</li><li>Experience with monitoring, logging, and platform observability.</li><li>Exposure to DevOps and CI/CD practices in restricted-network environments.</li></ul><h2>Candidate Profile</h2><p>The ideal candidate will be a hands-on technical engineer rather than purely an architectural or theoretical resource. They should be comfortable taking ownership of the deployment, administration, troubleshooting, and ongoing operational management of Hadoop and Spark platforms.</p><p>Candidates must be able to demonstrate practical experience working within environments where internet connectivity is restricted or unavailable, with an understanding of the additional complexities involved in deploying and maintaining enterprise data platforms in such environments.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/belmont-lavan-ltd/mainframe-data-engineer-3-to-6-months-contract-a