&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/flexport/software-engineer-ii-autonomous-supply-chains-amsterdam-120266","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795535739},{"slug":"commercial-account-executive-meta-amsterdam-300572","company_name":"Horizon3Ai","title":"Commercial Account Executive, META","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get to Know Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Horizon3.ai is a fast-growing, remote cybersecurity company dedicated to the mission of enabling organisations to proactively find and fix and verify exploitable attack vectors before criminals exploit them. Our flagship product,  the NodeZeroTM platform, delivers production-safe autonomous pentests and other key assessment operations that scale across the largest internal, external, cloud, and hybrid cloud environments. NodeZero has been adopted by organisations of all sizes, from small educational institutions to government agencies and Global 100 enterprises. It is used by ITOps/SecOps teams, consulting pentesters, and MSSPs and MSPs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a fusion of former U.S. Special Operations cyber operators, startup engineers, and formerly frustrated cybersecurity practitioners. We're committed to helping solve our common security problems: ineffective security tools, false positives resulting in alert fatigue, blind spots, "checkbox” security culture, cybersecurity skills shortage, and the long lead time and expense of hiring outside consultants. Collectively, we are a team of learn it alls, committed to a culture of respect, collaboration, ownership, and results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Description</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape the next stage of Horizon3.ai’s META growth. Based in the Netherlands with regular travel to the region, you’ll bring autonomous pentesting to new customers and help them reduce real-world security risk. If you thrive on opening doors, building partnerships and turning opportunities into wins, this is a chance to make a visible impact as we expand our META Commercial team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We currently require our Amsterdam team to come to the office 2 - 3 days per week. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What You’ll Do</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow Horizon3.ai’s META Commercial business by winning new customers, developing productive channel partnerships and helping organisations realise value from our cybersecurity solutions.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win new accounts and expand our customer base by introducing disruptive cybersecurity software solutions to the META market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and convert a qualified pipeline, owning the sales cycle from qualification and proof of value through negotiation and close, with the goal of exceeding quota consistently quarter over quarter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn channel partnerships into revenue by proactively engaging regional resellers and developing joint opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrate Horizon3.ai solutions in virtual and in-person meetings, connecting technical capabilities to customer needs and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the post-proof of value ROI process, helping customers understand business value while building relationships that support satisfaction and retention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate customer records, pipeline data and forecasts in Salesforce so opportunities, risks and next steps are clearly understood.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work independently to progress opportunities while collaborating with distributed sales, support and customer success teams to deliver a coordinated customer experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What You’ll Bring</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 3-5 years of successful cybersecurity sales experience, with a track record of driving growth, introducing disruptive software solutions and consistently exceeding quarterly quotas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous experience selling technical solutions into the META region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience establishing and monetising channel partnerships; existing relationships with key regional resellers are essential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency across the full sales process, including qualification, proof of value, forecasting, negotiation, deal closure and post-proof of value ROI management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to present and demonstrate cybersecurity solutions effectively, both virtually and in person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong CRM discipline and experience maintaining accurate pipeline records and forecasts in Salesforce (SFDC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Challenger Question-Based Selling-type methodologies and sales tools such as <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://outreach.io/">Outreach</a>, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, ZoomInfo and Slack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work independently and collaborate effectively with distributed teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English and Arabic; additional language skills such as French are welcomed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Travel Required</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a hybrid company, and this job will require you to spend 3 days based at our Amsterdam city centre sales hub. The role may require up to 40% of travel within the assigned territory to be successful. Job-related travel expenses are reviewed and must be approved by your manager.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks of </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai"><strong>Horizon3.ai</strong></a></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inclusive Team: We value diversity and promote an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth Opportunities: Be part of a dynamic and growing team with numerous career development opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Culture: Work in a collaborative environment that encourages creativity and out-of-the-box thinking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote Work: We are a 100% remote company. Enjoy the flexibility to work in the way that supports you and brings out your best.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Compensation: We offer competitive salary, equity and benefits. Our benefits include health, vision &amp; dental insurance for you and your family, a flexible vacation policy, and generous parental leave.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You Belong Here</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a> is not just an equal opportunity employer - we are a community that values diversity, equity, and inclusion as fundamental principles of our culture and success. We are dedicated to fostering a workplace where everyone feels welcome and respected, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, hair length or any other legally protected status by law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our commitment to diversity and inclusion means we strive to attract, develop, and retain a workforce that reflects the varied communities we serve. We believe that diverse perspectives drive innovation and strengthen our ability to create cutting-edge cybersecurity solutions. At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a>, every team member is valued and supported in an environment that encourages personal and professional growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome candidates from all backgrounds and experiences, and we encourage all qualified individuals to apply. Come be a part of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a>, where your unique contributions are recognized, and your potential is limitless.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Other Duties</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application Note</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/horizon3ai/commercial-account-executive-meta-amsterdam-300572","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1795534817},{"slug":"executive-assistant-team-experience-lead-amsterdam-288724","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Executive Assistant & Team Experience Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prosus is continuing to evolve its business, product and investment activities, with ambitious plans to build, scale and grow technology-driven businesses and products globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a highly organised, proactive and resourceful Executive Assistant to provide high-quality executive and operational support to three senior leaders: the Chief Product Officer, the Head of Ventures, and the Director of Strategy &amp; Operations.  This is a varied and fast-paced role that sits close to the heart of the business. You will play an important part in enabling these leaders to operate effectively, ensuring their time and priorities are managed efficiently and that the day-to-day running of their respective areas is seamless.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will take ownership of complex calendars, international travel, meeting preparation, stakeholder coordination and administrative processes, while anticipating needs, managing competing priorities and identifying opportunities to improve how things are done. Working across different teams and functions, you will build strong relationships throughout the organisation and act as a trusted point of contact for both internal and external stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for someone who combines exceptional organisational skills with sound judgement, discretion and a hands-on approach. Someone who enjoys being one step ahead, takes pride in making things happen and thrives in an environment where priorities can move quickly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><h3><strong>Executive &amp; Business Support</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide proactive, high-quality executive assistance to the Chief Product Officer, Head of Ventures, and Director of Strategy &amp; Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage complex and frequently changing calendars, prioritising meetings, resolving scheduling conflicts and ensuring leaders make the best use of their time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate domestic and international travel arrangements, including flights, accommodation, ground transportation, detailed itineraries and visa requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage meeting logistics, including scheduling, preparing agendas, coordinating pre-reads and ensuring relevant materials are available ahead of time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture key actions and follow up with relevant stakeholders to ensure commitments and deliverables are progressing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted first point of contact for internal and external stakeholders, handling requests with professionalism, sound judgement and discretion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively anticipate the needs of the executives, identifying potential scheduling conflicts, upcoming priorities and opportunities to improve efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage expenses, invoices, budget tracking and other administrative processes, ensuring accuracy and compliance with company policies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle confidential and sensitive information with the highest level of discretion and professionalism.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> <strong>Stakeholder &amp; Operational Coordination</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders across Product, Ventures, Strategy &amp; Operations and the wider Prosus organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate leadership meetings, workshops, offsites and other business events, managing logistics and ensuring smooth execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the coordination of cross-functional initiatives, helping ensure meetings, communications and follow-up actions are organised and delivered effectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with onboarding and administrative arrangements for new team members and other relevant stakeholders across the supported functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with HR, Finance, IT, Workplace, Legal and other internal teams to resolve requests and ensure efficient day-to-day operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to simplify administrative processes, improve ways of working and create greater efficiency for the executives and their teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide general operational support across the three functions, stepping in where needed to keep priorities moving and ensure nothing falls through the cracks.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a highly organised, proactive and solutions-oriented professional who enjoys working closely with senior leaders and making their lives easier.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You naturally think several steps ahead, have a strong sense of ownership and are comfortable managing multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment. You know when to take initiative, when to escalate and how to exercise sound judgement without needing constant direction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are confident in engaging with senior stakeholders, build relationships easily and communicate clearly and professionally. You are equally comfortable managing the finer details of a complex travel itinerary as you are coordinating a senior leadership meeting or resolving an unexpected scheduling challenge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Above all, you are dependable, discreet and take pride in delivering excellent support. You enjoy being behind the scenes, making things happen and creating the conditions for others to perform at their best.</p><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in an Executive Assistant, Senior Personal Assistant or Executive Business Partner role, ideally supporting multiple senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a fast-paced, international and complex business environment, preferably within technology, investment or a corporate organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple complex calendars and competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience coordinating international travel, meetings, leadership events and other executive-level logistics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the confidence to interact professionally with senior stakeholders and external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, hands-on mindset, with the ability to anticipate needs, solve problems independently and take ownership of tasks from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to detail and the ability to maintain accuracy while working at pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High levels of discretion, integrity and professionalism when handling confidential and sensitive information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across different teams and functions, building relationships and navigating a complex organisational environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Microsoft Office and other relevant productivity and collaboration tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English, both written and spoken.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/executive-assistant-team-experience-lead-amsterdam-288724","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795534817},{"slug":"program-manager-office-of-the-chief-product-officer-amsterdam-354679","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Program Manager, Office of the Chief Product Officer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The CPO office at Prosus is deliberately small. Nalden sets the direction: what we build and why. Jons, as Chief of Staff, creates the traction: the operating model, the portfolio, the prioritisation, and the decisions that turn direction into shipped product. Around them sit product managers, product marketing, growth, brand, content and design, and three product pods that do the building.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What holds those two ends together is the work itself: every initiative visible, owned and moving, and every decision captured before it evaporates. That is this job. As Program Manager you run Nalden_OS — the operating loop of the CPO portfolio — day to day. You do not own the initiatives; you make sure each one has someone who does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You join while that loop is being built rather than maintained, so you shape it: what gets tracked, how reviews run, what a decision record looks like, and which reporting we stop doing because nobody reads it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>In this role you will</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the whole portfolio visible, with an explicit owner on every line of work in flight across the CPO office and the product pods.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the decisions: shape ambiguous work until it is ready to be decided on, and prepare the prioritisation calls and operating reviews for the CPO and the Chief of Staff.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make it move: track progress and dependencies across teams, surface blockers early, and escalate with a recommendation rather than a status update.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make it stick: capture decisions and the reasoning behind them, keep the information people rely on accurate, and turn what teams learn into knowledge someone will reuse.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the view: a clean, reliable portfolio in slides, backed by a tracking system people actually update — assembled with AI so it takes an hour, not a week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the honest signal: say early where the plan and reality have diverged, including when the useful version is the uncomfortable one.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What This Role Is Not</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not make product decisions, approve teams' work, or become a reporting layer between teams and leadership. If teams spend more time updating you than shipping, the role is failing — and you would be the first to say so.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the person others trust in a messy week. When priorities shift and work stalls, you stay level, name what is actually happening, and get the loop closed. You follow up without nagging, and an unowned item bothers you until somebody picks it up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You like order, but you fit the system to the work rather than the other way round. You build trust quickly across designers, engineers and executives, and you carry influence without authority: you move work through people who do not report to you. You are direct enough to raise the awkward problem early, and low-ego enough to let someone else take the credit when it lands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8 to 10 years running cross-team program execution in digital commerce, technology product management, consumer facing technology, with an earlier career in management consulting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have owned outcomes across teams without owning the teams. Titles vary — program manager, strategy manager, operations lead, product operations — but the pattern is the same: you were accountable for work you moved through people who did not report to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in product work: you know how discovery, design and shipping actually run, and you can talk to designers and engineers without a translator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with data and tools: you build a clean portfolio view and a tracking system people trust, and you use AI to do the assembly faster than most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with senior leaders, ideally from an executive office or chief-of-staff environment; experience inside a larger corporate group around a small, fast team is a real advantage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable at both altitudes: you can run a room of executives in the morning and fix the tracking sheet in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and spoken English. Dutch is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a classic PMO profile. We want someone who clears the path, not someone who produces process.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global Impact: Play a crucial role in shaping the future of global commerce. Be part of a dynamic ecosystem of tech-led companies across markets, from emerging disruptors to established platforms, all working to create positive change at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth Opportunities: Expand your expertise through high-stakes challenges within our diverse portfolio. You will gain access to a network of businesses, leaders, and learning opportunities that span continents and industries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Culture: Join a forward-thinking team that values strategic insights and bold ideas. You will operate at the intersection of venture-building, innovation, and investment, where experimentation is encouraged and cross-company collaboration drives breakthroughs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creative Environment: Engage in work that encourages creativity and constant improvement. We challenge assumptions, explore new frontiers, and believe great ideas can come from anywhere in our ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative Atmosphere: Benefit from autonomy and self-management in a supportive, outcome-driven workspace. You will work alongside sharp, motivated peers across our portfolio, all united by a shared ambition to move the needle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid Work: Experience the satisfaction of our flexible model tailored to balance work and life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Compensation: Enjoy a salary package that reflects your skills and contributions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive Benefits: From health and wellness to learning, commuting, and everyday perks, we offer a well-rounded package designed to help you thrive at work and beyond.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/program-manager-office-of-the-chief-product-officer-amsterdam-354679","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795534817},{"slug":"senior-director-global-commissioning-handover-amsterdam-224550","company_name":"Volta","title":"Senior Director, Global Commissioning & Handover","description":"<h2><strong>About Volta</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is the category-defining, fully vertically integrated AI infrastructure platform – from capital to clusters to software, under a founder-led enterprise. Our mission is The Utility of Compute™: AI infrastructure as dependable and available as electricity, for every organization that needs it. Launched with a $10B strategic partnership with one of the leading frontier AI labs, a Series A led by Andreessen Horowitz, and a $5B AI Infrastructure Fund, Volta is building the infrastructure layer of the AI era from the ground up. We are 100+ people across London, Palo Alto, and New York, with rapid growth expectations to hundreds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commissioning is where an AI factory becomes real. As Senior Director, Global Commissioning &amp; Handover, you will lead commissioning of DSX facilities and network across all of Volta's sites, taking each one to ready for service and handing it over to our operations teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build and lead a global team that owns Volta's commissioning standards for electrical, mechanical and CDU scopes, systems security, commissioning planning, facilities readiness and operational readiness. Your team sets how commissioning is done on every site, from tagging through to the turn-up sequence, and holds the schedule that takes each facility live.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time to market matters here. You will align commissioning to the turn-up sequence so that commissioning accelerates service rather than delays it, and you will make sure that when a building is handed over, the operations team, the procedures and the systems are ready to run it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead commissioning of DSX facilities and network infrastructure across Volta's AI factories, taking each site to ready for service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the global Commissioning and Handover team, covering electrical, mechanical and CDU commissioning standards, systems security, commissioning planning, facilities readiness and operational readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Volta's commissioning standards for each discipline, from tagging and method statements through each commissioning level to the turn-up sequence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own CDU installation and commissioning standards, including handover to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the commissioning schedule for every site and its alignment to turn-up, so that commissioning is never the critical path to service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver the physical and systems security requirements for each site from construction through to handover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the facilities readiness and operational readiness standards and governance, so each facility is ready for operations and the operations team is ready to run it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead handover into service, working with DC Operations on acceptance, documentation and training.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Design and Engineering, the regional delivery teams and the DSX execution and network teams so commissioning is integrated into the master schedule on every site.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report commissioning progress and risk across sites, and feed lessons learned back into the standards and the reference design.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading commissioning of hyperscale data centres, including electrical, mechanical and liquid cooling systems. Data centre experience is essential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record owning commissioning and handover across multiple concurrent sites at this level, and the ability to run it from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of commissioning levels, integrated systems testing and the turn-up sequence for high density GPU environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CDU and liquid cooling commissioning and handover into operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience setting readiness governance and handing live facilities over to operations teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and leading commissioning teams and managing commissioning agents and contractors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of physical and systems security requirements in mission critical facilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel to sites across Europe and North America.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">REQ-263</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Volta, we believe people do their best work when they feel supported, trusted and able to grow. We're building a company where you can make an impact, keep a healthy balance between work and life, and build a career you're proud of. <br />As a global team, we do our best to provide great benefits wherever you're based. While some benefits vary by country due to local regulations, we believe looking after our people is simply the right thing to do.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on the work you do here, not your previous salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity in Volta, giving you the opportunity to share in the company's long-term success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement/pension contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive health, wellbeing and insurance benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous number of vacation days each year</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Additional Information</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Background Checks</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All offers of employment at Volta are conditional on the satisfactory completion of pre-employment screening, which includes confirmation of your right to work, verification of your employment history and a criminal record check, where this is permitted by local law. Screening is carried out by Zinc, an accredited third-party provider, after an offer is made and all information is handled confidentially and in accordance with applicable data protection law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Equal Opportunity</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team and make employment decisions based on skills, qualifications, experience and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected characteristic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Accessibility</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is committed to providing an accessible recruitment experience for all candidates. If you require accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the application or interview process, please contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="Hyperlink SCXW200826348 BCX0" ---------- We will work with you to identify reasonable accommodations that enable you to participate fully in the hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Candidate Privacy Notice</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">By applying, you consent to the processing of your personal data for recruitment purposes in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including the UK GDPR, EU GDPR and relevant US state privacy regulations. Your data will be shared only with those involved in the hiring process and will not be used for unrelated purposes. For details, see our Recruitment &amp; Candidate Privacy Notice.<br /></p><h3><strong>Note to Recruitment Agencies</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta does not accept unsolicited CVs or candidate profiles from recruitment agencies. Any unsolicited submissions, including those sent directly to hiring managers or employees, will be treated as the property of Volta. No agency fees will be payable unless a valid, signed recruitment agreement is in place, and the agency has been specifically engaged for the relevant vacancy.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £250K – £270K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li>United Kingdom • £250K – £270K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/volta/senior-director-global-commissioning-handover-amsterdam-224550","tags":["Delivery"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands - Remote","created_at":1795534816},{"slug":"senior-delivery-consultant-nl-amsterdam-50544","company_name":"Sig","title":"Senior Delivery Consultant","description":"<br><strong>Who we are </strong><p><p>Software Improvement Group (SIG) helpt organisaties grip te houden op de software waar hun business op draait. Ons platform Sigrid® bestaat uit twee delen. Sigrid Core geeft organisaties continu inzicht in de kwaliteit, security en risico’s van hun volledige softwareportfolio, en borgt kwaliteitsstandaarden tot in de ontwikkelstraat. Sigrid Axis, gelanceerd in oktober 2026, brengt diezelfde standaarden naar AI coding agents: het controleert elke wijziging die een agent maakt in real time en verbetert bestaande code, zodat organisaties agentic engineering kunnen opschalen zonder grip te verliezen op kwaliteit, kosten en risico. </p><p>Beide zijn gebouwd op ’s werelds grootste benchmark voor softwarekwaliteit, met meer dan 40.000 systemen en ruim 600 miljard regels code, en op ruim 25 jaar ervaring in het enige ISO/IEC 17025-geaccrediteerde lab voor softwarekwaliteit ter wereld. Samen met onze consultants vertalen we die inzichten naar strategisch en praktisch advies, zodat technologie een aanjager van succes is in plaats van een bron van risico. </p><p>Onze klanten zijn grote (internationale) ondernemingen, financiële instellingen en overheidsorganisaties. Zij vertrouwen op SIG om softwarekwaliteit structureel onderdeel te maken van de manier waarop ze hun IT-landschap besturen.</p></p><br><strong>Where you come in</strong><p><p>Als Senior Delivery Consultant zorg je ervoor dat onze grootste klanten Sigrid succesvol inbedden in hun organisatie. Sigrid is geen tool die je even installeert: het is complexe software voor kwaliteitsmanagement die raakt aan de ontwikkelstraat, de architectuur, de securityprocessen en de besluitvorming van een organisatie. Jij leidt die implementaties van begin tot eind: van kick-off en technische onboarding tot training, rapportage en de borging van softwarekwaliteit in de werkwijze van de klant. Of Sigrid nu als SaaS-oplossing wordt afgenomen of on-premise in de eigen infrastructuur van de klant draait, jij zorgt dat het project slaagt. </p><p>Dat maakt het werk uitdagend en cutting edge. Je werkt met technologie die vooroploopt, op het snijvlak van softwarekwaliteit en AI, bij organisaties die nu de stap zetten naar softwareontwikkeling met AI coding agents. Wat je bij hen implementeert, bepaalt mede hoe zij die stap veilig en beheerst kunnen maken. </p><p>Je werkt voor grote corporate organisaties en overheidsinstellingen, vaak met honderden ontwikkelteams en duizenden applicaties. Dat betekent complexe trajecten met veel belanghebbenden: van CIO en CISO tot architecten, IT-beheer, inkoop en ontwikkelteams. Je brengt structuur aan in die complexiteit, houdt planning en scope in de hand, en houdt de vaart erin zonder mensen kwijt te raken. </p><p>Je vertaalt de inzichten uit Sigrid naar rapportages en adviezen die passen bij je publiek. Een bestuurder wil weten waar de risico’s zitten, een architect wil technische schuld gericht aanpakken en een ontwikkelteam wil het dagelijkse werk verbeteren. Dezelfde data vertelt voor ieder van hen een ander verhaal, en jij weet die vertaalslag te maken. </p><p>Intern noemen we deze rol Senior Guidance Consultant. Je maakt deel uit van ons Guidance-team: een klein, hands-on team van consultants dat nauw samenwerkt met onze Customer Success Managers, Account Executives, technische consultants en het productteam. Na de implementatie draag je de klant over aan de Customer Success Manager, die de langetermijnrelatie voortzet. </p><br><p><strong><span style="font-size:18px;">Wat ga je doen </span></strong></p><ul><li>Je leidt complete implementatietrajecten waarin Sigrid wordt ingebed in grote organisaties, zowel SaaS als on-premise: van projectplan en kick-off tot technische onboarding, training en overdracht. </li><li>Je bent de projectleider: je bewaakt planning, scope en budget, managet risico’s en afhankelijkheden, en sluit aan op de governance van de klant, zoals stuurgroepen, security- en compliance-eisen en beheerprocessen. </li><li>Bij on-premise implementaties werk je samen met de infrastructuur- en securityteams van de klant en met onze technische consultants, zodat installatie, configuratie en integratie soepel verlopen. </li><li>Je begeleidt ontwikkelaars, architecten, managers en bestuurders bij het adopteren van Sigrid en het verankeren ervan in hun processen. </li><li>Je levert heldere rapportages en presentaties aan zowel management als technische doelgroepen, afgestemd op de doelen van de organisatie. </li><li>Je helpt klanten bij de inzet van Sigrid Axis, zodat hun AI coding agents werken volgens dezelfde kwaliteitsstandaarden als hun ontwikkelteams. </li><li>Je adviseert klanten over sturen op softwarekwaliteit, het beheersen van technische schuld en de verantwoorde inzet van AI in softwareontwikkeling. </li><li>Je managet meerdere trajecten tegelijk, gestructureerd en pragmatisch, inclusief een nauwkeurige projectadministratie in ons CRM. </li><li>Je ondersteunt salestrajecten met overtuigende productdemo’s en met je inbreng over implementatieaanpak en planning. </li></ul><p>Je draagt bij aan de doorontwikkeling van onze implementatiemethodiek, onze Academy-content en de ondersteuning van partners die zelf Sigrid-implementaties uitvoeren. </p><br><br></p><br><strong>What's in it for you?</strong><p><ul><li><p>Een betekenisvolle rol op het snijvlak van technologie, consultancy en organisatieverandering </p></li><li>Directe impact bij enkele van de grootste organisaties van Nederland, in het bedrijfsleven en bij de overheid </li><li>Een platte organisatie met ruimte voor ondernemerschap, initiatief en creativiteit </li><li>Een grondig inwerkprogramma in onze tooling en methodiek, en ruimte voor je persoonlijke ontwikkeling </li><li>Flexibele werkafspraken en een betrokken team van hoog niveau </li><li>Goede secundaire arbeidsvoorwaarden, waaronder een mobiele telefoon, MacBook en verzekeringen </li></ul><p>Wij geloven dat software beter kan en moet bijdragen aan de organisaties waarin het draait. Deel jij die overtuiging en wil je helpen die waar te maken? Dan horen we graag van je. </p></p><br><strong>Job Requirements</strong><p><p>Je bent een senior professional die sterk projectmanagement combineert met plezier in klantcontact. Je hebt eerder complexe projecten geleid binnen grote organisaties en weet hoe je resultaat boekt in een omgeving met veel belanghebbenden, wisselende prioriteiten en formele besluitvorming. </p><ul><li>Minimaal vijf jaar ervaring in een klantgerichte rol als implementatieconsultant, projectmanager of vergelijkbaar </li><li>Aantoonbare ervaring met het leiden van complexe projecten, bij voorkeur de uitrol van een SaaS- of on-premise softwareoplossing bij grote corporate klanten en/of overheidsorganisaties </li><li>Ervaring met de governance van grote organisaties: je weet hoe stuurgroepen, inkoop-, security- en beheerprocessen werken en hoe je daarbinnen voortgang boekt </li><li>Een projectmanagementcertificering (zoals PRINCE2, PMP of IPMA) is een plus; bewezen praktijkervaring weegt het zwaarst </li><li>Affiniteit met softwareontwikkeling, softwarekwaliteit en technische schuld; je voert het gesprek net zo makkelijk met ontwikkelaars als met bestuurders </li><li>Uitstekende beheersing van het Nederlands in woord en geschrift, en daarnaast goed Engels </li><li>Heldere, overtuigende communicatie, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk </li><li>Een flexibele, pragmatische houding, gecombineerd met een gestructureerde en zorgvuldige manier van werken </li><li>Werk- en denkniveau op masterniveau </li></ul><p>Je bent woonachtig in Nederland en mag hier werken zonder dat je nu of in de toekomst sponsoring door een werkgever nodig hebt. </p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/sig/senior-delivery-consultant-nl-amsterdam-50544","tags":["Analytical Skills","Presentation Skills","Software Development","Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)","Software Engineers","Computer Science","Project Management","Software Developmen","Interpersonal Communication","Project Management Training","Direct Client Interaction","Customer Interaction","Customer Software Implementation"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"NL - Amsterdam","created_at":1795534369},{"slug":"marketing-specialist-benelux-nordics-zaandam-321436","company_name":"Jumbo","title":"Marketing Specialist (Benelux & Nordics)","description":"Do you want to have an excellent experience as an employee in one of the most pioneering <strong>toy companies</strong> in the market? Are you passionate about games and driven to provide exceptional products and services to customers worldwide?<br><br>This is the company you are looking for!<br><br>At Jumbo Group, we are not just an international company; we are an international playground. Our world is filled with games, puzzles, and toys that spread joy and inspire creativity across the globe. We enjoy a robust presence throughout Europe and in all corners of the world.<br><br><strong>About the role</strong><br><br>Are you ready to make our brands shine – both online and offline? As Marketing Specialist, you’ll take full ownership of a selection of Jumbo’s brands across the Benelux and Nordics. From strategy to execution, from campaign concept to retail catalogue — you’ll manage your brands full journey. <br><br>You translate global brand strategies into local plans that drive awareness, engagement and sales at retail. You’ll also make sure your brands perform at their best on all online platforms.<br><br>In this dynamic role, you’ll work closely with the Marketing Manager, the local Sales teams, Product Development, the global Brand team, and the local eCommerce manager. Together, you’ll make sure Jumbo’s brands are top of mind for retailers and consumers– no two days are the same.<br><br><strong>What you’ll be working on:</strong><br><br><strong>Brand & Campaign Management</strong><br><br>· Take ownership of your brand portfolio in Benelux & Nordics.<br><br>· Translate global brand strategies into local brand plans and activation strategies.<br><br>· Manage the local assortment: know your products inside out, select the right new launches together with commercial team, and ensure the best fit for your markets.<br><br>· Be a sparring partner for local and global teams, bringing in fresh ideas and creativity and ensure alignment across markets.<br><br>· Monitor brand performance, track results and adjust plans accordingly. Share insights with the sales teams and global team.<br><br>· Create and manage impactful campaigns, events & retail activations (ATL and BTL) in close collaboration with sales and e-commerce.<br><br>· Work closely with creative, media, influencer, social media and activation agencies.<br><br>· Create presentations and sell-in decks for sales, retailers and partners.<br><br>· Communicate plans, updates and best practices clearly across internal teams and external partners.<br><br><strong>E-Commerce & Digital Marketing</strong><br><br>· Ensure strong online visibility and conversion for your brands through optimised product content.<br><br>· Execute retail media campaigns and product activations on Bol.com, Amazon and other key online partners, together with the local e-com manager.<br><br>· Align your brand presence across Jumbo’s local social channels in collaboration with our SoMe agency and fellow Marketing Specialists.<br><br>· Share and apply digital insights and best practices across markets.<br><br><strong>What you bring to the team</strong><br><br>· Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Marketing, Communication, Business Administration, Digital Commerce, or a related field.<br><br>· Minimum of 2–4 years of experience in Marketing, Brand Management, Trade Marketing or Digital Marketing.<br><br>· Hands-on with e-commerce platforms (Bol.com, Amazon or similar) and retail media campaigns.<br><br>· Affinity with social media management and content creation.<br><br>· Analytical and organisational skills; confident with Excel, PowerPoint and analytics tools.<br><br>· Experience in the toy, entertainment, or FMCG sector is a plus, but not mandatory.<br><br><strong>What makes you a great fit</strong><br><br>· You’re a strong multitasker who loves variety – product launches, campaigns, activations, all in one week? Bring it on!<br><br>· A creative storyteller with fresh ideas and an eye for detail.<br><br>· A confident communicator in Dutch & English; French or a Nordic language is a plus.<br><br>· A collaborative, hands-on team player who enjoys making things happen.<br><br>· Passion for toys & games – you know how to turn play into impact.<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/jumbo/marketing-specialist-benelux-nordics-zaandam-321436","tags":["Strategic Marketing"],"job_types":["Contract","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zaandam","created_at":1795540655},{"slug":"accountmanager-bouw-waterdichting-rotterdam-459597","company_name":"AV Werving & Selectie","title":"Accountmanager Bouw - Waterdichting","description":"<p>Nederland</p><p>Een commerciële buitendienstfunctie waarin jij zelf een markt opbouwt, met de slagkracht van een internationale producent achter je. Bij IKO krijg je de vrijheid om jouw eigen commerciële koers te bepalen, hoogwaardige technische oplossingen te verkopen en zichtbaar bij te dragen aan groei. Een zelfstandige baan voor een ondernemende accountmanager die kansen ziet én benut!</p><h2>Maak het verschil als Accountmanager Bouw – Waterdichting in Nederland</h2><p>Dankzij jouw commerciële daadkracht groeit IKO's positie in de Nederlandse markt voor vloeibare waterdichting. Je ontwikkelt zelfstandig nieuwe klantrelaties en brengt hoogwaardige oplossingen onder de aandacht bij onder andere aannemers, voorschrijvers, woningcorporaties en vastgoedbeheerders. Denk aan waterdichtingstoepassingen voor balkons, galerijen, parkeerdaken en -dekken, dakdetails en brugdekken. Je onderzoekt de markt, signaleert bouw- en renovatieprojecten en weet op het juiste moment de juiste gesprekspartners te bereiken. Daarbij verkoop je op technische meerwaarde en bouw je aan langdurige samenwerkingen. Je start met een kleine bestaande klantenportefeuille en richt je aanvankelijk op new business om jouw portefeuille verder uit te breiden. Je bent regelmatig onderweg naar klanten en projecten, werkt verder regelmatig vanuit huis en bent uiteraard welkom op het kantoor in Klundert. Je schakelt met jouw Nederlandse en Belgische salescollega's en technische specialisten.</p><h2>Kortom, jij pakt de regie bij het:</h2><ul><li><p>zelfstandig ontwikkelen van de Nederlandse markt voor vloeibare waterdichting;</p></li><li><p>actief benaderen van nieuwe klanten, waaronder aannemers, voorschrijvers en andere potentiële opdrachtgevers;</p></li><li><p>signaleren en opvolgen van commerciële kansen binnen bouw-, renovatie- en infrastructurele projecten;</p></li><li><p>adviseren over hoogwaardige technische oplossingen en opbouwen van duurzame klantrelaties;</p></li><li><p>ontwikkelen van een sterke salespipeline en zorgvuldig vastleggen van commerciële activiteiten in Salesforce (CRM).</p></li></ul><h2>Als gedreven Accountmanager Bouw – Waterdichting kun jij rekenen op:</h2><p>Een zelfstandige commerciële functie bij een internationaal familiebedrijf waar ondernemerschap en eigen initiatief worden gewaardeerd. IKO biedt je de ruimte om jouw markt te ontwikkelen, ondersteund door ervaren collega's en technische specialisten. Tijdens jouw inwerkperiode leer je bovendien van het Belgische salesteam.</p><h2>Op basis van een fulltime dienstverband krijg je daarbovenop:</h2><ul><li><p>een competitief salaris, passend bij jouw kennis en ervaring;</p></li><li><p>een bonusregeling tot 10% van jouw jaarsalaris;</p></li><li><p>25 vakantiedagen + 12 ATV dagen;</p></li><li><p>een auto, laptop en telefoon van de zaak;</p></li><li><p>een pensioenregeling volgens Hibin;</p></li><li><p>veel vrijheid om jouw eigen agenda en commerciële activiteiten te organiseren;</p></li><li><p>de mogelijkheid om regelmatig vanuit huis te werken;</p></li><li><p>toegang tot kennis en expertise binnen een internationale organisatie.</p></li></ul><h2>Voor deze vacature neem jij mee:</h2><p>Jij krijgt energie van het openen van deuren en het ontwikkelen van nieuwe commerciële kansen. Je neemt initiatief, werkt gestructureerd en houdt koers tijdens langdurige verkooptrajecten. Met jouw nieuwsgierigheid en technische interesse achterhaal je de werkelijke klantbehoefte. Je schakelt gemakkelijk tussen verschillende gesprekspartners, van uitvoerende aannemers tot technisch adviseurs, en weet hen met inhoudelijke argumenten te overtuigen.</p><h2>Vink jij deze checklist ook af?</h2><ul><li><p>mbo+/hbo werk- en denkniveau;</p></li><li><p>minimaal 3 tot 5 jaar commerciële buitendienstervaring, bij voorkeur als accountmanager of technisch-commercieel adviseur;</p></li><li><p>aantoonbare ervaring met directe verkoop aan aannemers en actieve acquisitie;</p></li><li><p>technische affiniteit, bij voorkeur met bouwproducten, waterdichting, coatings of infrastructurele toepassingen;</p></li><li><p>ervaring met CRM-systemen, bij voorkeur Salesforce, en goede kennis van Excel.</p></li></ul><h2>Jouw werkgebied</h2><p>Jouw werkgebied beslaat heel Nederland, met een focusgebied in de driehoek Rotterdam, Utrecht en Amsterdam. Je werkt veel vanuit huis en bezoekt zelfstandig klanten, prospects en projecten. Je deelt jouw agenda grotendeels zelf in en stemt afspraken af op de commerciële kansen in jouw regio. Regelmatig heb je contact met collega's op de Nederlandse vestiging in Klundert. Voor trainingen en salesmeetings bezoek je incidenteel het Europese hoofdkantoor in Antwerpen.</p><h2>Werken bij IKO</h2><p>IKO is een internationaal familiebedrijf en producent van hoogwaardige dakbedekkings-, isolatie- en waterdichtingsoplossingen. Ze zijn marktleider en staan voor kwaliteit. Met circa 4.000 medewerkers wereldwijd levert de organisatie technische producten voor uiteenlopende bouw- en infrastructuurprojecten.</p><p>Binnen de productgroep IKO flexia ligt de focus op vloeibare waterdichting voor specialistische toepassingen, binnen dit segment zijn wij op zoek naar een nieuwe collega.</p><p>De organisatie is actief in meer dan 40 landen en heeft haar Europese hoofdkantoor in Antwerpen. IKO werd in 1951 opgericht in Canada en is nog altijd een echt familiebedrijf. De cultuur is nuchter, lean en hands-on: een ‘doe’-mentaliteit met veel vrijheid, eigen verantwoordelijkheid en korte lijnen.</p><h2>Eén klik verwijderd van jouw nieuwe baan</h2><p>Gaat jouw hart sneller kloppen van deze vacature en heb je de checklist afgevinkt? Wacht dan niet te lang, want zodra wij een geschikte kandidaat hebben gevonden sluiten we de vacature. Solliciteren doe je simpel en snel via onze solliciteer-button. Vergeet je niet om een up-to-date cv en een gerichte motivatie toe te voegen? Heb je vragen over de vacature? Neem dan contact op met Achraf via telefoonnummer 06-13402694 of mail naar ----- Misschien spreken we elkaar dan snel!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/av-werving-selectie/accountmanager-bouw-waterdichting-rotterdam-459597","tags":["Sales Engineer"],"job_types":["Tijdelijk contract","professional / ervaren"],"location":"Rotterdam","created_at":1795705362},{"slug":"backend-engineer-amsterdam-197303","company_name":"Catawiki","title":"Backend Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Catawiki, every day brings the extraordinary! Whether it’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Daniel Ricciardo’s Formula 1 Car&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/579-fossils&quot;&gt;Woolly Mammoth’s Skeleton&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/l/10035805&quot;&gt;Lady Gaga&#39;s Jumpsuit&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Usain Bolt’s running shoe&lt;/a&gt;, we encounter exceptional objects every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a one-of-a-kind marketplace for buying and selling special objects. Each week, more than 100,000 unique items are auctioned, all carefully curated by our passionate in-house experts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Having sold over 25 million unique objects, our mission is to become the world’s most popular destination for special objects. As a growing, diverse and sustainable scale-up, we proudly live by three core values. If these values resonate with you, we’d love to explore how you can join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ownership and driving impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being open to change and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being passionate about our mission and our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our path to becoming the most visited online curated marketplace for special objects, our Engineering team is on a mission to deliver the best experience across our platforms by building best-in-class products for search and discovery, bidding, curation, logistics, payments, and support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a scale-up tackling customer-facing challenges at high scale, with 75,000 auctions per week and more than 10 million visitors per month. As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Backend Engineer&lt;/em&gt;, you’ll support one of our three verticals - &lt;strong&gt;Demand&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Supply&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;Fulfilment&lt;/strong&gt; - improving and delivering product innovations for our platform.&lt;br&gt;Working in a small, fully autonomous, and highly collaborative Agile team, you will build scalable, maintainable, and resilient microservices and features. That’s why we’re looking for developers who share ideas, explore options, and communicate openly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be part of a team with end-to-end responsibility for its own microservices, collaborating across disciplines to build, operate, and continuously improve our products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt; by designing, developing, testing, deploying, maintaining, and improving scalable microservices and features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own what you deliver&lt;/strong&gt;, taking responsibility for the quality, resilience, and maintainability of your team’s services throughout their lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across disciplines&lt;/strong&gt; while closely working with product designers, product owners, and frontend, backend, and mobile engineers to share ideas and deliver product innovations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve how we work&lt;/strong&gt;, identifying opportunities to make our engineering processes more effective and efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen our engineering culture&lt;/strong&gt; by documenting and advocating for development best practices across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise product quality&lt;/strong&gt; by fixing bugs and refactoring the codebase where necessary to keep our products reliable and maintainable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and experiment&lt;/strong&gt; by testing new technologies and participating in Technical Week - a week dedicated to creativity, innovation, and knowledge sharing across domains after every two product sprints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand the full lifecycle of web development, identify opportunities, explore solutions, and keep customer needs at the center of your work. Our stack is mainly focused on Ruby; however, prior Ruby experience is not essential if you’re passionate about learning new things.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Strong software engineering foundations&lt;/span&gt;: 7+ years of software development experience, specifically with object-oriented programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Relevant product experience&lt;/span&gt;: 3+ years of experience working with customer-facing products in industries such as e-commerce, fintech, or SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Backend service expertise&lt;/span&gt;: Experience designing, implementing, and deploying backend services with a focus on high availability, low latency, and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;API and data knowledge&lt;/span&gt;: A good understanding of API design, SQL, and relational databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Clear communication&lt;/span&gt;: Excellent English communication skills and comfort raising concerns, sharing ideas, and documenting your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Collaborative mindset&lt;/span&gt;: You contribute to the team, take initiative, and step in to help when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Solution-oriented thinking&lt;/span&gt;: You actively identify opportunities and explore alternative approaches to solving problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Commitment to growth&lt;/span&gt;: You take ownership of developing your skills by learning new technologies and seeking new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our engineers work in small, fully autonomous, and highly collaborative Agile teams aligned with one of three verticals: Demand, Supply, or Fulfilment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teams are responsible for their own microservices from design and development through deployment, maintenance, and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineers collaborate closely with product designers, product owners, and frontend, backend, and mobile colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We value bold thinking, curiosity, openness, initiative, and a strong customer focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Week creates dedicated space for experimentation, creativity, innovation, and knowledge sharing across domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Where You&#39;ll Be&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;em&gt;Hybrid&lt;/em&gt; role based in Amsterdam. &lt;strong&gt;You will work from our &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Amsterdam HQ&lt;/span&gt; a minimum of 2 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At this time, we are only considering candidates who are already based in&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;the &lt;strong&gt;Netherlands&lt;/strong&gt;. As a result,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;relocation support is not available for this position&lt;/span&gt;. We can, however, &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;provide visa transfer from current Dutch employer&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;In Return&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be part of an enthusiastic, highly motivated team of &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;800+ Catawikians&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;A competitive &lt;u&gt;Annual Gross Base Salary&lt;/u&gt; depending on your level, competencies, and overall experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;A &lt;u&gt;Work From Home Allowance&lt;/u&gt; to help with your monthly household bills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Commuting&lt;/u&gt; between your home and our office is covered by Catawiki.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Amazing &lt;u&gt;Office&lt;/u&gt; right in the centre of Amsterdam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;text text-align-left &quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working with Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a visible impact &lt;/strong&gt;by working at scale in a global organisation serving millions of customers across 80+ categories. In our flat structure, every role has a broad scope and directly impacts both our customers and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and grow&lt;/strong&gt; through our Learning &amp;amp; Development initiatives, including clear development plans and mentorship programmes to support your career progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A culture of connection defines us&lt;/strong&gt;. We’re a passionate, diverse team of 800+ Catawikians representing 60+ nationalities. We foster an inclusive and queer-friendly environment where everyone is encouraged to bring their full self to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Celebrate life’s moments with us. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll receive a €100 Catavoucher when you join, a €50 Catavoucher on your birthday, and an extra day off each year to “Pursue Your Passion&lt;strong&gt;”&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer additional leave for key work anniversaries and important life events. Benefits may vary by location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Offices and Way of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Our vibrant offices in Amsterdam and Lisbon are designed to inspire collaboration. Most Catawikians operate in a hybrid setup, combining office-based and remote work, with a minimum of two days per week in the office, unless a role is explicitly stated as fully remote or fully office-based.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interested?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Apply with an English CV and Cover Letter. By applying, you agree to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/conditions/applicant-privacy-policy.pdf&quot;&gt;Catawiki’s Applicant Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support the review of your application. AI may help us assess how your experience matches the requirements of the role, but hiring decisions are always made by our recruitment team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/catawiki/backend-engineer-amsterdam-197303","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795524916},{"slug":"regulatory-compliance-officer-amsterdam-312668","company_name":"Mollie","title":"Regulatory Compliance Officer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2004, we've had one clear goal: to make payments and money management effortless for every business in Europe. Today, more than 250,000 companies use Mollie to get paid, manage money and grow – with products designed to be simple, scalable, and dependable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 950+ Mollies across 14+ locations, we care deeply about autonomy and craft. So we work in small teams, with real ownership, and we trust you to make the right decisions. We're building for the long term, so we provide the tools you need, processes you can rely on, and a balanced work environment to help you do work you're proud of.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound like your kind of place? Let's build together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Your impact</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compliance at Mollie is a competitive advantage — and you'll be the one building it. As a Regulatory Compliance Officer, you'll be at the heart of how we scale responsibly across Europe, turning complex regulatory requirements into practical, automated solutions that actually work for the business. You'll own the frameworks, lead the conversations, and make sure compliance moves at the same pace we do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also lead and develop a team of junior and mid-level compliance officers — coaching them, reviewing their work, and helping them grow. Your expertise across AML/CFT, sanctions, and regulatory advisory will set the standard for how the team operates and how compliance is embedded across Mollie.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role where your work has real reach. The frameworks you build, the policies you shape, and the culture you foster will directly support over 350,000 businesses growing with less friction and more freedom.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What you'll ship</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A robust, scalable compliance framework across AML/CFT, sanctions, and governance — designed to support Mollie's rapid European expansion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, actionable policies and controls that translate PSD2/3, AMLD6 and EBA Guidelines into practical business requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive risk assessments and thematic reviews that identify and close compliance gaps before they become problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compliance embedded into product development lifecycles — working closely with Product, Engineering, Legal, Risk, and Operations to make it happen by design, not as an afterthought</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-quality regulatory reporting and senior management deliverables, prepared with precision and delivered on time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A stronger, more capable compliance team — through structured mentorship, coaching, and quality oversight that raises the bar across the board</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h3><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of compliance experience within a regulated financial institution — Fintech, PSP, EMI, or (neo)bank</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong, hands-on knowledge of European regulatory frameworks, including PSD2, AMLD, EBA Guidelines and/or MiCAR</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid experience across both financial crime (AML/CFT, sanctions) and broader regulatory compliance advisory</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to translate complex regulations into clear, practical solutions — without overcomplicating it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the confidence to challenge and influence senior leadership when it matters</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of mentoring or managing junior compliance professionals and elevating team performance</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Grow your way</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Mollie, growth is personal. We believe everyone should have the chance to develop their skills, explore new challenges and shape their career on their own terms. You'll get regular feedback and performance reviews to support your development, with fair and transparent salary reviews along the way. Many Mollies move into new roles or take on new projects to stretch themselves, and we actively hire from within to help you take the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No matter if you're aiming for promotion, exploring a different career path or building new skills, you'll be supported with the tools, trust and opportuni