s you to be the best version of yourself.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>We are Metyis. Partners for Impact.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>A great organization with a strong culture, shaped by the diversity of our colleagues</p></li><li><p>A pragmatic, growing company where your work makes a visible difference</p></li><li><p>Direct contact with the people you support and with business leadership</p></li><li><p>A varied role across two organizations, Metyis and Adaptfy, with an international network of HR colleagues</p></li><li><p>A team who actively invests in your development</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>Handle day-to-day HR operations for Metyis: onboarding week and offboarding, contracts and employee changes, absence management, documentation, and employee questions</p></li><li><p>Advise leadership and employees on people matters, from performance conversations and employee relations to engagement, and help translate insights into practical actions while challenging where needed</p></li><li><p>Support leadership discussions by bringing relevant people insights, priorities, and actions to the table</p></li><li><p>Ensure compliance with Dutch employment law and translate global policies into practical procedures for Metyis</p></li><li><p>Run HR cycles such as performance management</p></li><li><p>Contribute to cross-functional and international HR projects across Metyis</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>What you will bring</h2><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>A bachelor’s degree in human resources or a related field; a master’s degree is a plus</p></li><li><p>5+ years of HR experience, ideally in international, scale-up, consulting or professional services environments</p></li><li><p>Solid knowledge of Dutch employment law experience in both HR advice and operations</p