&lt;p&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing reasonable support (called accommodations or adjustments) in our recruiting processes for candidates who are differently abled, have long term conditions, mental health conditions or sincerely held religious beliefs, or who are neurodivergent or require pregnancy-related support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/zscaler/sales-account-executive-enterprise-107552","tags":["EMEA Field Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795449325},{"slug":"internal-communications-internship-amsterdam-324364","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Internal Communications Internship","description":"<h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Internal Communications Intern, you’ll join our Marketing &amp; Communications team and help keep colleagues across SkyNRG informed, connected and engaged. Working closely with our PR &amp; Communications Manager and teams across the business, you’ll create engaging content, support internal campaigns and events, and help improve the channels and tools we use to communicate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Content creation:</strong> Draft and publish newsletters, intranet articles, announcements, interviews, employee stories and leadership updates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employee engagement:</strong> Support internal campaigns, company events and town halls that connect and engage colleagues across SkyNRG.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Channels &amp; tools:</strong> Maintain internal communication channels and content calendars and help improve the processes and tools behind them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work with teams across the organization to gather information and turn it into clear and engaging communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Insights &amp; improvement:</strong> Monitor engagement and use insights to continuously improve our internal communications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You recognize yourself in the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Current Bachelor’s or Master’s studies in Communications, Public Relations, Journalism, Marketing, Business or a related field, with enrollment for the full duration of the internship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to create clear and engaging content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong interest in internal communications, employee engagement and organizational culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple activities simultaneously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work independently and collaboratively with colleagues across different teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Microsoft 365 tools, including Teams, Outlook, PowerPoint and SharePoint.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-time availability for a 6-month internship from 15 February 2027 onwards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration is fundamental to achieving our ambition. We nurture genuine relationships with global partners in our drive to make SAF <em>the</em> alternative to fossil jet fuel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our in-house team of SAF experts have helped over 60 airlines and corporates reduce their climate impact using the Book &amp; Claim mechanism; the most transparent and traceable way to support aviation sustainability with real emission reductions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability is woven into the fabric of our company. We maintain an independent Sustainability Board, which advises the company on feedstocks and provides strategic guidance on wide-ranging sustainability issues. SkyNRG operations are certified against the RSB EU RED, CORSIA, and Book &amp; Claim standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At SkyNRG, you’ll find:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovation-driven culture – where big ideas turn into real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities – in a fast-scaling, industry-changing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team – where your ideas and expertise are valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission that matters – leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high-integrity SAF</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a brand-new office in the heart of Amsterdam, designed for collaboration and creativity. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a truly game-changing green initiative, making a real impact on the aviation industry and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Besides that, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A unique working experience in a scale-up at the forefront of sustainable aviation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An inspiring international work environment in a fast growing and innovative industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A great opportunity to work in a multidisciplinary, committed, and talented team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work where it feels best for you: we offer flexible (hybrid in-office/remote) working arrangements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A monthly internship allowance of 800 euros.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuting travel reimbursement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid Volunteering Day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our electric company boat, free lunches, and social activities – all part of the deal!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Is this you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your career with SkyNRG? Explore our vacancies and become part of our company of change makers. Together, we can change the future of flying.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information about SkyNRG visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>📌 Please note: We do not accept sales inquiries or intermediary services.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At SkyNRG, we deeply value inclusion and diversity. As an equal opportunity employer, we are dedicated to ensuring every applicant has a fair chance, irrespective of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected characteristics.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitn